          "convergenceTargetId": "1773671580308",
          "id": "1772743618879",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772743618880_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{!($context.$variables.userSessionObject.priceList?.PriceListId != null  && $context.$variables.userSessionObject.priceList?.PriceListId !== \"\"  && $context.$variables.userSessionObject.priceList?.PriceListItems?.length > 0  && $context.$variables.userSessionObject.priceList?.PriceListItems?.[0]?.InventoryItemId != null  && $context.$variables.userSessionObject.priceList?.PriceListItems?.[0]?.InventoryItemId !== \"\")}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6215.237272821884,
            "y": 6265.408100888803
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Parse Input Intend to extract key data",
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              }
            }
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772717544024"
          },
          "code": "PARSE_INPUT_INTEND_TO_EXTRACT_KEY_DATA",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772743764010",
          "id": "1772709290468",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772709290469_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "AI Extractor Prompt: Balance Management Configuration Metadata Extraction.\n\n1. JSON OUTPUT SCHEMA (MANDATORY FORMAT) \n\nOutput ONLY a single valid JSON, with no extra text, markdown, or comments. Omit any field entirely if inapplicable; use null only for truly unknown values.\nWhen errorMessage is populated because required details are missing, still return every value that can be derived from userMessage, userFile, or userSessionObject in the JSON structure below. \nDo not discard partially provided data just because the response needs an errorMessage. \n   For example, if the user provides the consumption model type, set priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.RatingModel to the matching ORA_OSS_* value even when other required fields are missing and errorMessage is non-null.\nIf the user provides only the consumption model type and other required details are missing, still construct the minimum nested output path needed to store it: priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.RatingModel. Use existing priceList, PriceListItems, and ratePlans from userSessionObject when available. Do not invent unknown PriceListName, Item, RatePlanName, BalanceProfileName, BalanceCode, charges, or entitlement detail values; omit unknown fields and explain the missing details in errorMessage.\n\nOptional ID pass-through rule:\nInventoryItemId, PriceListItemId, RatePlanId, and RatePlanChargeId, UsageEntitlementNumber,UsageEntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanNumber are optional pass-through fields only.\nIf the exact non-empty value exists in userSessionObject at the same corresponding row, copy it to the output.\nIf the value is missing, null, blank, or unavailable in userSessionObject, omit the field entirely.\nDo not validate these fields, do not ask the user for these fields, do not set errorMessage because these fields are missing, and never invent or derive them from userMessage or userFile.\n\njson\n{\n   priceList : {\n      PriceListName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\",\n      PriceListItems : [\n         {\n            Item: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\",\n            InventoryItemId: \"<must be taken from userSessionObject priceList.PriceListItems[].InventoryItemId  if present, if not omit this attribute>\",\n            PriceListItemId: \"<must be taken from userSessionObject priceList.PriceListItems[].PriceListItemId  if present, if not omit this attribute>\",\n            PricingUOM: \"<derive from userSessionObject if it exists, if not from userMessage or userFile>\",\n            ratePlans: [\n               {\n                  RatePlanName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                  RatePlanId: \"<must be taken from userSessionObject only when present. If RatePlanId is missing, null, or empty, omit RatePlanId from the output object entirely. Never output RatePlanId: null.\",\n                  ratePlanCharges: [\n                     {\n                        RatePlanChargeId: \"<must be taken from userSessionObject only when present. If RatePlanChargeId is missing, null, or empty, omit RatePlanChargeId from the output charge object entirely. Never output RatePlanChargeId: null.\",\n                        chargeName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\", \n                        price: \"<derive numeric price from the same charge phrase. Supports decimals and currency before or after the number, e.g. $0.5 or 0.5$. Never round/truncate decimal values.>\",\n                        pricePeriod: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Only for recurring charges. Empty for usage charge.>\",\n                        chargePeriod: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. For usage charge, if not mentioned take from allowancePeriodicity>\",\n                        quantityAttribute: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile.>\"|null,\n                        quantityUOMAttribute: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile.>\"|null,\n                        allowManualAdjustments: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Set to one of these values 'Y' if manual adjustments are allowed or 'N' if manual adjustments are not allowed. If nothing is mentioned default to 'N'>\"|null,\n                        usageUnitOfMeasure: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile when the same usage charge row explicitly provides a usage UOM, even when chargePeriod is also populated; otherwise omit>\",\n\n                     }\n                  ],\n                  entitlementPlan: {\n                     UsageEntitlementNumber: \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If UsageEntitlementNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit UsageEntitlementNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output null\">,\n                     UsageEntitlementPlanNumber: \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present.  If UsageEntitlementPlanNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit UsageEntitlementPlanNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output UsageEntitlementPlanNumber: null.\">,\n                     EntitlementPlanNumber: \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If EntitlementPlanNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit EntitlementPlanNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output EntitlementPlanNumber: null.>\",\n                     EntitlementPlanName: \"<use same value as RatePlanName>\"|null,\n                     BalanceProfileName: \"<derive only from explicit Balance Profile phrases, such as 'Balance Profile <name>', 'BalanceProfileName <name>', or 'Use Balance Profile <name>'. Do not derive from pooling, pool, customer account level, account level, customer level. If not explicitly provided, omit BalanceProfileName and add errorMessage asking for Balance Profile.>\",\n                     BalancePoolingCriteria: \"<temporary helper only. Derive from pooling phrases only when BalanceProfileName cannot be directly extracted. If BalanceProfileName is populated, omit BalancePoolingCriteria from the final output. Never output BalancePoolingCriteria together with BalanceProfileName.>\",\n                     RatingModel: <derive from userMessage if its Allowance(ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE), Estimate (ORA_OSS_ESTIMATE), Commitment(ORA_OSS_COMMITMENT) or Volume Pricing (ORA_OSS_VOLUME_PRICING) model. Set to one of these values ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE|ORA_OSS_ESTIMATE|ORA_OSS_COMMITMENT|ORA_OSS_VOLUME_PRICING accordingly. If no mention of allowance, estimate, commitment or volume pricing model explicity, populate errorMessage asking user details of consumption model (allowance/estimate/commitment/volume pricing) is to be provided politely\">,\n                     allowances: [\n                        {\n                           chargeName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\",\n                           BalanceCode: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for terms Balance Code and extract name. If no explicit Balance Code phrase is present, derive from allowance wording like 'allowance of <quantity> <balance-code-name> <unit>' by removing the quantity and unit and using the remaining descriptor as BalanceCode.>\",\n                           balanceCategory: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for terms category. Do not assume. If not mentioned, leave empty.>\"|null,\n                           quantity: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile >\"|null,\n                           quantityUOM: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                           amount: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                           amountCurrency: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                           allowancePeriodicity: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for a period mentioned along with the allowance quantity or amount and remove terms like 'per' >\"|null,\n                           allowanceValidityPeriod: \"<derive the numeric count of the allowance validity period from userMessage or userFile. Must always be a number. If the user says 'a quarter', 'a year', 'one quarter', 'per quarter', 'valid for a quarter', 'quarterly', or provides a period unit without an explicit numeric count, set allowanceValidityPeriod = 1. Do not convert quarter or year to another unit unless the user explicitly says 3 months or 12 months..etc. If it cannot be determined, set to 1>\",\n                           allowanceValidityPeriodUOM: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Normalize period units to lowercase singular values such as day, week, month, quarter, or year. For 'a quarter', 'one quarter', 'per quarter', 'valid for a quarter', or 'quarterly', use quarter. Do not pair allowanceValidityPeriod = 3 with allowanceValidityPeriodUOM = quarter; use 1 + quarter, or only use 3 + month when the user explicitly says 3 months.>\",\n                           rolloverPeriod: \"<derive only when userMessage or userFile explicitly states a rollover duration/count or rollover frequency, such as rollover for 3 months, rollover period of 1 year, rollover yearly, rollover monthly, or roll over weekly. For rollover frequency without a numeric count, set rolloverPeriod = 1. Do not use estimate periods, usage periods, charge periods, price periods, or billing periods. If user only says rollover enabled without a rollover duration/frequency, leave empty/null>\"|null,\n                           rolloverPeriodUOM: \"<derive only when rolloverPeriod has a value and the unit/frequency is explicitly tied to rollover. Map rollover daily->day, weekly->week, monthly->month, quarterly->quarter, yearly/annually/annual->year. Do not use units from estimated usage, usage charge billing, recurring charge billing, price period, or charge period. If rolloverPeriod is empty/null, leave empty/null>\"|null\n                        }\n                     ],\n                     estimates: [\n                        {\n                           chargeName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Pick charge if mentioned estimates based on when mentioned.>\",\n                           BalanceCode: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for terms Balance Code and extract name. Do no assume>\",\n                           quantity: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile >\"|null,\n                           quantityUOM: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                           amount: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                           amountCurrency: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                           relatedChargeName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Pick other than whats picked for chargeName.>\",\n                           trueupShortfall: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile having values true|false>\",\n                           trueupOverage: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile having values true|false>\",\n                           enableRollOver: \"<set true if userMessage or userFile explicitly mentions rollover enabled/enable rollover/roll over/rollover. Set false only when rollover is not mentioned or when the user explicitly disables rollover. This flag can be true even when rolloverPeriod and rolloverPeriodUOM are empty/null>\",\n                           rolloverPeriod: \"<derive only when userMessage or userFile explicitly states a rollover duration/count or rollover frequency, such as rollover for 3 months, rollover period of 1 year, rollover yearly, rollover monthly, or roll over weekly. For rollover frequency without a numeric count, set rolloverPeriod = 1. Do not use estimate periods, usage periods, charge periods, price periods, or billing periods. If user only says rollover enabled without a rollover duration/frequency, leave empty/null>\"|null,\n                           rolloverPeriodUOM: \"<derive only when rolloverPeriod has a value and the unit/frequency is explicitly tied to rollover. Map rollover daily->day, weekly->week, monthly->month, quarterly->quarter, yearly/annually/annual->year. Do not use units from estimated usage, usage charge billing, recurring charge billing, price period, or charge period. If rolloverPeriod is empty/null, leave empty/null>\"|null\n                        }\n                     ],\n                     commitments: [\n                        {\n                           chargeName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Pick charge if mentioned commitments based on when mentioned.>\",\n                           period:  \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\",\n                           BalanceCode: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for terms Balance Code and extract name. Do no assume>\",\n                           relatedChargeName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile more than one usage charge mentioned. Pick other than whats picked for chargeName.>\",\n                           quantity: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile >\"|null,\n                           quantityUOM: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                           amount: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                           amountCurrency: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null\n                        }\n                     ],\n                     volumePricing: [\n                        {\n                           chargeName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Pick charge if mentioned volume pricing based on when mentioned.>\",\n                           aggregationPeriod: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Pick period for the chargeName>\",\n                           BalanceCode: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for terms Balance Code and extract name. Do no assume>\",\n                           EligibilityFlag: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for eligible volume pricing and set boolean true or false if not mentioned accordingly.>\",\n                           EligibilityBalanceCode: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for Balance Code mentioned along with eligibile for volume pricing and extract name. Do no assume. Only set when EligibilityFlag is true, otherwise clear.>\"|null,\n                           AggregationFlag: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for eligible aggregation and set boolean true or false if not mentioned accordingly.>\",\n                           AggregationBalanceCode: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for Balance Code mentioned along with eligibile for aggregation and extract name. Do no assume. Only set when EligibilityFlag is true, otherwise clear.>\"|null\n                        }\n\n                     ],\n                     unitOfMeasureConversions:[\n                        {\n                           chargeName: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile with context of uom (unit of measure) conversion.>\",\n                           BalanceCode: \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for terms Balance Code and extract name. Do no assume>\",\n                           sourceUOM:  \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for terms source unit of measure or source UOM>\",\n                           conversionRate:  \"<derive from userMessage or userFile. Look for terms conversion rate. Only numeric value.>\",\n                           startDate:  \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null,\n                           endDate:  \"<derive from userMessage or userFile>\"|null\n                        }\n                     ]\n                  }\n               }\n            ]\n         }\n      ]\n   },\n  errorMessage : \"<If attribute PriceListName or Item or BalanceProfileName or BalanceCode doesnt have a value or if either ratePlanCharges doesnt have a chargeName;\n                     If RatingModel=ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE and  allowances also requires chargeName, BalanceCode, period and periodUOM along with either a quantity with quantityUOM or amount with amountCurrency;\n                     If RatingModel=ORA_OSS_ESTIMATE and  estimates also requires chargeName, BalanceCode, relatedChargeName, chargePeriod and relatedChargePeriod along with either a quantity with quantityUOM or amount with amountCurrency;\n                     If RatingModel=ORA_OSS_COMMITMENT and  commitments also requires chargeName, BalanceCode and aggregationPeriod;\n                     If RatingModel=ORA_OSS_VOLUME_PRICING and  volumePricing also requires chargeName, BalanceCode and period along with either a quantity with quantityUOM or amount with amountCurrency;\n                  Set with a user friendly message asking user for that attributes.\n                  Never ask for optional pass-through identifiers in errorMessage: InventoryItemId, PriceListItemId, RatePlanId, RatePlanChargeId, UsageEntitlementNumber, UsageEntitlementPlanNumber, or EntitlementPlanNumber. These are not required business inputs. If they are missing from userSessionObject, omit them silently. Do not mention them even with phrases like 'if available', 'for complete configuration', or 'please provide'.>\"|null,\n  firstTimeModelGenerated: boolean,\n  retreiveDataCollection: array\n}\n\n2. RUNTIME VARIABLES (DO NOT MODIFY VARIABLE NAMES OR FORMAT)\n   Current Input (userMessage): {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n   User Provided Attachment (userFile): {{$context.$nodes.RETREIVE_USER_PROVIDED_DATA_FOR_PROCESSING.$output}}\n   User session object (userSessionObject): {{$context.$variables.userSessionObject}} \n\n3. GENERAL EXTRACTION & NORMALIZATION RULES \n   Price list maintenance scope guard:\n     Before any extraction, check whether the userMessage or userFile asks to create a new price list, add an item/product/offering directly to a price list, or otherwise maintain price list setup itself.\n     If so, do not perform the requested price list maintenance action and set errorMessage exactly to: \"I am unable to perform that action currently, as its outside my scope. Could you do that externally\"\n     Do not trigger this guard when the user only asks to create a rate plan, entitlement, allowance, estimate, commitment, or volume pricing model using an existing price list.\n     Do not trigger this guard for one-time charges, recurring charges, usage charges, base price, charge period, or related charge details that are part of the requested rate plan.\n\n   UOM handling\n     Treat PricingUOM and usageUnitOfMeasure as user-provided text fields only.\n     Do not default, infer, normalize, uppercase, lowercase, or synthesize a UOM value when it is not explicitly present in userMessage or userFile.\n     If a UOM is not explicitly stated, omit that field instead of using a common default such as Each.\n     Do not convert user-provided UOM text into a UOMCode in this prompt.\n   \n   rolloverPeriod:\n      - Set only when the user explicitly provides a rollover duration/count OR a rollover frequency.\n      - Valid duration examples: \"rollover for 3 months\", \"rollover period is 1 year\", \"roll over unused balance for 2 weeks\".\n      - Valid frequency examples: \"rollover yearly\", \"rollover annually\", \"rollover monthly\", \"rollover quarterly\", \"rollover weekly\", \"rollover daily\".\n      - For rollover frequency without a numeric count, set rolloverPeriod = 1.\n      - If the user only says rollover enabled/enable rollover/rollover without a duration or frequency, leave rolloverPeriod empty/null.\n      - Do not borrow periods from estimated usage, usage charge billing, recurring charge billing, price period, or charge period. For example, in \"estimated usage of 1200 prints per year rollover enabled\", set enableRollOver=true and leave rolloverPeriod empty/null. In \"estimated usage of 1200 prints per year rollover yearly\", set enableRollOver=true, rolloverPeriod=1, rolloverPeriodUOM=\"year\".\n\n   rolloverPeriodUOM:\n      - Only set when rolloverPeriod has a value and the unit/frequency is explicitly tied to rollover.\n      - Normalize explicit rollover units/frequencies to lowercase singular nouns: day, week, month, quarter, year.\n      - Map daily->day, weekly->week, monthly->month, quarterly->quarter, yearly/annually/annual->year.\n      - Do not use period units from estimated usage, usage charge billing, recurring charge billing, price period, or charge period.\n   \n   RatingModel explicit intent rule:\n      - Do not infer RatingModel from charge names, pricing charge definitions, or labels such as \"Allowance Monthly Charge\".\n      - If userSessionObject already contains extracted priceList/ratePlans data and the current userMessage only answers the missing consumption model type, preserve every existing value from userSessionObject exactly as-is and update only priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.RatingModel to ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE, ORA_OSS_ESTIMATE, ORA_OSS_COMMITMENT, or ORA_OSS_VOLUME_PRICING respectively. Clear the missing-consumption-model errorMessage when the RatingModel is set.\n      - If the user explicitly provides the consumption model type along with incomplete or missing other data, set priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.RatingModel to the matching ORA_OSS_* value and also populate errorMessage for the remaining missing details. A non-null errorMessage must not prevent RatingModel or any other available extracted fields from being returned in the defined output format.\n      - Explicit model type phrases must set RatingModel even when entitlement details are incomplete:\n        allowance model, allowance consumption model, model is allowance, use allowance -> ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE\n        estimate model, estimate consumption model, model is estimate, use estimate -> ORA_OSS_ESTIMATE\n        commitment model, commitment consumption model, model is commitment, use commitment -> ORA_OSS_COMMITMENT\n        volume pricing model, model is volume pricing, use volume pricing -> ORA_OSS_VOLUME_PRICING\n      - Also set RatingModel = ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE when the user explicitly describes an allowance entitlement, such as \"30 mins allowance\", \"allowance per month\", or \"allowance of $100\" and clear only the missing-consumption-model error.\n      - If allowance/estimate/commitment/volume pricing appears only inside a charge name, treat RatingModel as missing.\n      - When RatingModel is missing, set errorMessage to: \"Please specify the consumption model type: Allowance, Estimate, Commitment, or Volume Pricing.\"\n      - That errorMessage is allowed only when RatingModel is missing, null, blank, or not one of the supported values.\n   Price extraction:\n      Extract decimal prices exactly. Valid price patterns include \"$100\", \"100$\", \"$0.5\", \"0.5$\", \"0.50 dollars\", and \"0.5 per minute\".\n      Preserve decimal values; do not round, truncate, or convert 0.5 to 0.\n      For each charge row, derive price only from the price phrase closest to that same charge name.\n\n   allowances\n     Combine recurring charges (chargeName having periodicity like montly..etc) and charge based allowance record into one.\n       Choose chargeName from the recurring charge allowance\n       rest of the attributes come from the charge based allowance record. \n       Populate quantity/quantityUOM for quantity-based; amount/amountCurrency for amount-based.\n       allowanceValidityPeriod must always be numeric. If userMessage or userFile does not provide a determinable numeric value, set allowanceValidityPeriod = 1.\n       Omit irrelevant fields as per rules except for BalanceCode.\n     During updated user can refer to this object as an allowance.\n      Switch from using quantity/quantityUOM for quantity based or amount/amountCurrency for amount-based.\n      If user mentioned a quantity with a unit of measure, clear amount/amountCurrency and use quantity/quantityUOM.\n         For allowance quantity phrases, always extract quantityUOM from the unit token immediately after the numeric quantity.\n         Pattern: \"<quantity> <quantityUOM> allowance per <period>\".\n            Example: \"30 Each allowance per Month\" => quantity = \"30\", quantityUOM = \"Each\", allowancePeriodicity = \"Month\".\n            Example: \"100 Color per month\" => quantity = \"100\", quantityUOM = \"Color\", allowancePeriodicity = \"month\".\n         Trust the token immediately after the allowance quantity as quantityUOM exactly as provided, after trimming punctuation. Do not reject it merely because it also matches BalanceCode or is not found in setup data.\n      Rollover-only phrases must not create additional allowance rows. If the user has already provided one allowance for the same BalanceCode and chargeName, attach rolloverPeriod/rolloverPeriodUOM details from phrases like \"unused <BalanceCode> will roll over for <period>\" to that existing allowance row only.\n      If an existing allowance row already has rolloverPeriod and rolloverPeriodUOM from a closer explicit phrase such as \"it rollsover 2 months\", do not create a second allowance row for another rollover-only phrase. Preserve the existing rollover values unless the user clearly says to change or override them.\n      If user mentions a value with a currency or currency symbol, clear quantity/quantityUOM and populate amount/amountCurrency accordongly.\n   estimates\n     Combine recurring charges (chargeName having periodicity like montly..etc) or usage charge and charge based estimate (chargeName having usage) record into one.\n       Choose chargeName from the usage charge.\n       Populate quantity/quantityUOM for quantity-based; amount/amountCurrency for amount-based.\n       Choose relatedChargeName from the recurring charge (or usage charge if not recurring).\n       Omit irrelevant fields as per rules except for BalanceCode.\n   commitments\n     Combine recurring charges (chargeName having periodicity like montly..etc) or usage charge and charge based estimate (chargeName having usage) record into one.\n       Choose chargeName from the usage charge.\n       Populate quantity/quantityUOM for quantity-based; amount/amountCurrency for amount-based.\n       Omit irrelevant fields as per rules except for BalanceCode.\n\n     During updated user can refer to this object as an estimate.\n      Switch from using quantity/quantityUOM for quantity based or amount/amountCurrency for amount-based.\n      If user mentioned a quantity with a unit of measure, clear amount/amountCurrency and use quantity/quantityUOM.\n      If user mentions a value with a currency or currency symbol, clear quantity/quantityUOM and populate amount/amountCurrency accordongly.\n   \n   rolloverPeriod:\n      Extract numeric rollover count only from a phrase explicitly tied to rollover duration or frequency.\n      If rollover frequency is stated without a numeric count, such as rollover yearly/monthly/quarterly/weekly/daily, set rolloverPeriod = 1.\n      If rollover is only enabled and no rollover duration/frequency is stated, leave rolloverPeriod empty/null.\n      Do not use \"per year\", \"billed yearly\", \"billed monthly\", or similar estimate/charge/billing periods as rolloverPeriod unless that period is explicitly part of the rollover phrase.\n   rolloverPeriodUOM:\n      Extract rollover unit only from a phrase explicitly tied to rollover duration or frequency.\n      For rollover yearly/annually/annual set rolloverPeriodUOM = \"year\"; monthly = \"month\"; quarterly = \"quarter\"; weekly = \"week\"; daily = \"day\".\n      If rolloverPeriod is empty/null, leave rolloverPeriodUOM empty/null.\n      Do not use estimate/charge/billing period units as rolloverPeriodUOM unless explicitly part of the rollover phrase.\n   enableRollOver:\n      - Set true if rollover enabled/enable rollover/roll over/rollover is mentioned in userMessage or userFile.\n      - Set true if rolloverPeriod has a value.\n      - Set true if rolloverPeriodUOM has a value.\n      - Set false only when rollover is not mentioned, or when the user explicitly disables rollover.\n      - Never output enableRollOver=false when rolloverPeriod or rolloverPeriodUOM is populated.\n      - enableRollOver can be true while rolloverPeriod and rolloverPeriodUOM are empty/null when the user enabled rollover but did not specify a rollover duration/frequency. If the user says rollover yearly/monthly/quarterly/weekly/daily, set enableRollOver=true and populate rolloverPeriod/rolloverPeriodUOM accordingly.\n\n   Strict RatingModel gating\n     If RatingModel = ORA_OSS_ESTIMATE, entitlementPlan.allowances, entitlementPlan.volumePricing and entitlementPlan.commitments must be [] and only entitlementPlan.estimates may be populated.\n     If RatingModel = ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE, entitlementPlan.estimates, entitlementPlan.volumePricing and entitlementPlan.commitments must be [] and only entitlementPlan.allowances may be populated.\n     If RatingModel = ORA_OSS_COMMITMENT, entitlementPlan.allowances, entitlementPlan.volumePricing and entitlementPlan.estimates must be [] and only entitlementPlan.commitments may be populated.\n     If RatingModel = ORA_OSS_VOLUME_PRICING, entitlementPlan.allowances, entitlementPlan.commitments, entitlementPlan.unitOfMeasureConversions and entitlementPlan.estimates must be [] and only entitlementPlan.volumePricing may be populated.\n     Do not populate more than one array for the same entitlementPlan.\n     \n     unitOfMeasureConversions is only valid when RatingModel is ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE or ORA_OSS_ESTIMATE or ORA_OSS_COMMITMENT.\n        set entitlementPlan.unitOfMeasureConversions = [], when RatingModel = ORA_OSS_VOLUME_PRICING.\n\n\n4. FIELD EXTRACTION GUIDELINES \n     PriceListName:\n        Extract from userMessage (if not present, check in userFile)  if not already in userSessionObject.\n        Look for terms Price List or Price list name. \n\n        If userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListId is present, use it.\n        If not, extract from userMessage using the following guidelines:\n         Search userMessage for any of the following (case-insensitive):\n            “Price List”, “Pricelist”, “Price List Name”, “List Name”, “PL Name”, “Price Sheet”\n         Extract value immediately following the matched phrase, supporting connectors:\n            after “is”, “:”, “=”, “named”, or inside quotes/brackets\n         Use regex if available:\n            (?i)(Price[\\s_-]*List(Name)?|Pricelist|PL Name|List Name|Price Sheet)[\\s:=\\-\"\\']+(?P<name>[A-Za-z0-9_ \\-]+)\n         On error, look for above phrases in userFile\n         If still not found, omit field and set errorMessage with a polite prompt, e.g.,\n            \"Which Price List would you like to create the consumption model under?\"\n         Broaden logic to tolerate extra spaces, basic typos (e.g., 'pricelist', 'price listt', etc.), and punctuation.\n\n     Item :\n         Extract from userMessage (if not present, check in userFile) if not already in userSessionObject.\n         Look for terms Item, Item Name, Product, Product Name, Offering, Offering Name.\n         If user says \"for offering <value>\", \"offering <value>\", \"for item <value>\", or \"for product <value>\", extract <value> as Item.\n         Preserve quoted or parenthesized text exactly. Example: for offering “Printer as Service (Allowances)” => Item = \"Printer as Service (Allowances)\".\n         Do not treat \"for offering <value> in <PriceListName>\" as price list maintenance; it is valid item extraction for the consumption model.\n         If response after message which Item, take that as value.\n         If Item cannot be determined, populate errorMessage with a user friendly message which Item would the user like to create the consumption model under. Add reference to PriceListName if it has been determined.\n     PricingUOM :\n         Extract from userMessage (if not present, check in userFile) if not already in userSessionObject.\n         Look for explicitly provided unit terms such as Each, Dozen, Box, Pack, Case, User, and similar UOM text.\n         Populate only when the user explicitly states a pricing unit of measure.\n         If not found, omit field. Do not default to Each.\n\n     ratePlans:\n      Match on plan, subscription, or rate descriptions; append ' Plan' to RatePlanName if not already present.\n      Add recurring and/or one-time charges if applicable.\n      Add an entitlementPlan for a ratePlan.\n      Copy RatePlanName to  EntitlementPlanName.\n      For recurring and/or one-time charge, add allowances.\n      Add appropriate allowance quantity and its unit to quantityUOM or amount and its currency to amountCurrency.\n      Also match period where present.\n      Populate usageUnitOfMeasure when the user explicitly provides a usage unit for the same usage charge row.\n      If usageUnitOfMeasure is not explicitly provided, omit it. Do not use Each or any other default.\n      For usage charges, usageUnitOfMeasure may be populated even when chargePeriod is also populated.\n         Example: \"billed monthly at 0.5$ per each\" => chargePeriod = \"month\", usageUnitOfMeasure = \"each\".\n      Do not put usage UOM values such as each, minute, minutes, GB, or hours into quantityAttribute.\n      Do not ask for manual adjustment confirmation; if manual adjustment is not mentioned, default allowManualAdjustments to \"N\" or omit it.\n\n      BalanceProfileName:\n         Extract from userMessage (if not present, check in userFile) if not already in userSessionObject.\n         Extract only from explicit terms BalanceProfileName, Balance Profile, Balance Profile Name, or Use Balance Profile.\n         Do not use values from pooling phrases, including \"customer account level\", \"account level\", \"customer level\", \"pool at\", or \"pooling at\".\n         If BalanceProfileName cannot be determined, populate errorMessage with a user friendly message which BalanceProfile would the user like to create the usage rating entitlement for.\n     \n     BalancePoolingCriteria:\n         Use BalancePoolingCriteria only as a temporary hint to help identify BalanceProfileName when the user provides pooling/profile wording but not an explicit Balance Profile.\n         If BalanceProfileName is populated from userMessage, userFile, or userSessionObject, omit BalancePoolingCriteria from the final output.\n         Never output both BalanceProfileName and BalancePoolingCriteria.\n         For phrases like \"pooling profile is Print\", set BalanceProfileName = \"Print\" and omit BalancePoolingCriteria.\n         For phrases like \"pool at customer account level\", use the phrase only as a hint if needed; do not output BalancePoolingCriteria when BalanceProfileName has a value.\n\n     BalanceCode :\n         Extract from userMessage (if not present, check in userFile) if not already in userSessionObject.\n         Look for terms BalanceCode, Balance Code, Balance Code Name. \n         If the user says \"performance guarantee on <value>\", \"guarantee on <value>\", \"estimated usage on <value>\", \"allowance of <quantity> <value> <unit>\", \"includes an allowance of <quantity> <value> <unit>\", or similar, derive BalanceCode from <value>.\n         For allowance quantity phrases, remove the numeric quantity and UOM/unit words such as minute, minutes, min, mins, hour, hours, each, unit, units, GB, MB, dollars, or currency names. Keep the remaining descriptor exactly as the BalanceCode.\n         Example: \"The plan includes an allowance of 100 SmartHand minutes per month\" => BalanceCode = \"SmartHand\".\n         If BalanceCode cannot be determined, populate errorMessage with a user friendly message which BalanceCode would the user like to create the usage rating entitlement allowance for.\n     \n     true-up toggle rules\n      trueupOverage and trueupShortfall are mutually exclusive unless the user explicitly asks to enable both.\n      If the user says overage only, overage above estimated usage, or equivalent:\n         set trueupOverage = true\n         set trueupShortfall = false\n      If the user says shortfall only, shortage only, below estimated usage only, or equivalent:\n         set trueupShortfall = true\n         set trueupOverage = false\n      If the user explicitly disables both true-up overage and true-up shortfall:\n         set trueupOverage = false\n         set trueupShortfall = false\n         append to errorMessage:\n         \"Either trueup overage or trueup shortage needs to be enabled\"\n      If the user does not mention true-up behavior, set trueupShortfall = true and trueupOverage = true.\n\n     errorMessage\n         If attribute PriceListName or Item or BalanceProfileName or BalanceCode doesn't have a value or if either ratePlanCharges or allowances doesn't have a chargeName. allowances also requires period and periodUOM along with either a quantity with quantityUOM or amount with amountCurrency Set with a user friendly message asking user for that attributes.\n         When setting errorMessage, still preserve and output all data already provided or derived in the mandatory JSON format. Do not return only errorMessage. Keep priceList, PriceListItems, ratePlans, entitlementPlan, RatingModel, charges, allowances, estimates, commitments, volumePricing, and unitOfMeasureConversions fields that can be populated from userMessage, userFile, or userSessionObject.\n         If the user has provided the model type, set priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.RatingModel even when errorMessage is also populated for other missing required data.\n         If only RatingModel can be extracted, return that RatingModel at the nested entitlementPlan path and set errorMessage for the missing details. Do not replace the structured output with only errorMessage.\n         Do not populate errorMessage for fields that have already been extracted as non-empty values.\n         If BalanceCode is non-empty, do not ask the user to confirm Balance Code.\n         If an allowance has quantity and quantityUOM, do not ask the user to confirm quantity unit of measure. This includes quantityUOM values extracted from the token immediately after the allowance quantity, even when that token equals BalanceCode.\n         If an allowance has allowancePeriodicity, treat the allowance period as provided.\n         If an allowance has allowanceValidityPeriod and allowanceValidityPeriodUOM, treat validity period details as provided.\n         Never create a new allowance row only because a sentence mentions rollover, roll over, unused balance, or unused <BalanceCode>. Merge those rollover details into the existing matching allowance row, and do not set an errorMessage for a missing quantity/amount on the rollover-only sentence.\n         Do not ask for manual adjustment details when they are not mentioned.\n         Never include InventoryItemId, PriceListItemId, RatePlanId, RatePlanChargeId, UsageEntitlementNumber, UsageEntitlementPlanNumber, or EntitlementPlanNumber in errorMessage. These are optional pass-through fields only. If missing, omit them silently.\n         Never ask the user to provide or confirm manual adjustment details. If allowManualAdjustments is missing, default it to \"N\" or omit it.\n         Never ask the user to confirm quantity unit of measure when quantityUOM is already non-empty, including values such as Each, each, minute, minutes, GB, or hours.\n         Before returning JSON, review errorMessage. If errorMessage asks only for optional pass-through identifiers, set errorMessage = null. If errorMessage includes optional pass-through identifiers along with real missing business fields, remove the optional identifier text and keep only the real missing business-field requests.\n         Use user friendly terms, like instead of \n            1. ratePlanCharges use Rate Plan Charges.\n            2. chargeName use Charge\n            3. allowances use Entitlement details.\n         Combine messages only for missing required business fields, excluding optional pass-through IDs, manual adjustment fields, and fields already extracted as non-empty values.\n     firstTimeModelGenerated\n         Extract value from userSessionObject and set the value.\n     retreiveDataCollection\n          Extract value from userSessionObject and set the value.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"priceList\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"PriceListName\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"PriceListId\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\"\n        },\n        \"PriceListItems\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"Item\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              \"InventoryItemId\": {\n                \"type\": \"integer\"\n              },\n              \"PriceListItemId\": {\n                \"type\": \"integer\"\n              },\n              \"ratePlans\": {\n                \"type\": \"array\",\n                \"items\": {\n                  \"type\": \"object\",\n                  \"properties\": {\n                    \"RatePlanId\": {\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                    \"RatePlanNumber\": {\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                    \"RatePlanName\": {\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                    \"ratePlanCharges\": {\n                      \"type\": \"array\",\n                      \"items\": {\n                        \"type\": \"object\",\n                        \"properties\": {\n                          \"RatePlanChargeId\": {\n                            \"type\": \"string\"\n                          },\n                          \"chargeName\": {\n                            \"type\": \"string\"\n                          },\n                          \"price\": {\n                            \"type\": \"integer\"\n                          },\n                          \"pricePeriod\": {\n                            \"type\": \"string\"\n                          },\n                          \"chargePeriod\": {\n                            \"type\": \"string\"\n                          },\n                          \"quantityAttribute\": {\n                            \"type\": \"string\"\n                          },\n                          \"quantityUOMAttribute\": {\n                            \"type\": \"string\"\n                          },\n                          \"usageUnitOfMeasure\": {\n                            \"type\": \"string\"\n                          }\n                        }\n                      }\n                    },\n                    \"entitlementPlan\": {\n                      \"type\": \"object\",\n                      \"properties\": {\n                        \"UsageEntitlementNumber\": {\n                          \"type\": \"string\"\n                        },\n                        \"UsageEntitlementPlanNumber\": {\n                          \"type\": \"string\"\n                        },\n                        \"EntitlementPlanNumber\": {\n                          \"type\": \"string\"\n                        },\n                        \"EntitlementPlanName\": {\n                          \"type\": \"string\"\n                        },\n                        \"BalanceProfileName\": {\n                          \"type\": \"string\"\n                        },\n                        \"BalancePoolingCriteria\": {\n                          \"type\": \"string\"\n                        },\n                        \"RatingModel\": {\n                          \"type\": \"string\"\n                        },\n                        \"allowances\": {\n                          \"type\": \"array\",\n                          \"items\": {\n                            \"type\": \"object\",\n                            \"properties\": {\n                              \"BalanceCode\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\"\n                              }\n                            }\n                          }\n                        },\n                        \"estimates\": {\n                          \"type\": \"array\",\n                          \"items\": {\n                            \"type\": \"object\",\n                            \"properties\": {\n                              \"BalanceCode\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\"\n                              }\n                            }\n                          }\n                        },\n                        \"commitments\": {\n                          \"type\": \"array\",\n                          \"items\": {\n                            \"type\": \"object\",\n                            \"properties\": {\n                              \"BalanceCode\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\"\n                              }\n                            }\n                          }\n                        },\n                        \"volumePricing\": {\n                          \"type\": \"array\",\n                          \"items\": {\n                            \"type\": \"object\",\n                            \"properties\": {\n                              \"BalanceCode\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\"\n                              }\n                            }\n                          }\n                        },\n                        \"unitOfMeasureConversions\": {\n                          \"type\": \"array\",\n                          \"items\": {\n                            \"type\": \"object\",\n                            \"properties\": {\n                              \"BalanceCode\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\"\n                              }\n                            }\n                          }\n                        }\n                      }\n                    }\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"errorMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
