        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Understand User input for Rate Plan and its Entitlements"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776799007265"
          },
          "code": "UNDERSTAND_USER_INPUT_FOR_RATE_PLAN_AND_ITS_ENTITLEMENTS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772793479984",
          "id": "1772788320840",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772788320841_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "AI Extractor Prompt: Manage Consumption Model Setup Configuration Extract\n\nRUNTIME VARIABLES (DO NOT MODIFY VARIABLE NAMES OR FORMAT)\n    1. Current Input (user message): {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n    2. User Provided Attachment (user file): {{$context.$nodes.RETREIVE_USER_PROVIDED_DATA_FOR_PROCESSING.$output}}\n    3. User session object (userSessionObject): {{$context.$variables.userSessionObject}}\n    4. Existing pricing charge definitions (pricingChargeDefinitions) : {{$context.$nodes.RETREIVE_SETUP_DATA.$output.result.pricingChargeDefinitions}}\n    5. Existing Balance Codes (balanceCodes) : {{$context.$nodes.RETREIVE_SETUP_DATA.$output.result.balanceCodes}}\n    6. Existing Balance Profiles (balanceProfiles) : {{$context.$nodes.RETREIVE_SETUP_DATA.$output.result.balanceProfiles}}\n    7. Existing Units of measure (unitsOfMeasureList) : {{$context.$nodes.RETREIVE_SETUP_DATA.$output.result.unitsOfMeasureList}}\n    8. Existing Pricing Period Units of measure (pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList) : {{$context.$nodes.RETREIVE_SETUP_DATA.$output.result.pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList}}\n    9. Existing Time Units of measure (timeUnitsOfMeasureList) : {{$context.$nodes.RETREIVE_SETUP_DATA.$output.result.timeUnitsOfMeasureList}}\n    10. Existing Balance Categories (balanceCategoriesList) : {{$context.$nodes.RETREIVE_SETUP_DATA.$output.result.balanceCategories}}\n    11. CurrentDate (YYYY-MM-DD): {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} \n\nGENERAL EXTRACTION & NORMALIZATION RULES \n    Output object rule:\n      Return a JSON object, not a JSON string. Do not wrap the entire JSON output in quotes. Do not escape the whole object as text.\n      The first non-whitespace character of the response must be { and the last non-whitespace character must be }.\n      Do not include markdown fences, comments, prose, or explanatory text before, after, inside, or next to JSON fields.\n      Do not place explanations inside field values. If a key must be omitted, physically omit the key entirely.\n\n    No explanatory placeholder values rule:\n      Never output text such as \"missing, so omitted\", \"in userSessionObject is missing\", \"not available\", \"no RatePlanId is present, so omit\", or similar as a JSON field value.\n      Optional IDs and optional fields with no valid source value must be absent from the returned JSON, not present with null, comments, or explanatory text.\n      Every emitted JSON value must be the actual business value, boolean, number, object, array, or null only when explicitly allowed by the field rules.\n\n    Optional identity fields insertion rule:\n      The following fields are optional identity fields, not required skeleton fields:\n      RatePlanId, RatePlanChargeId, UsageEntitlementNumber, UsageEntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanDetailNumber,\n\n      When the exact non-empty value exists in userSessionObject at the same corresponding row, add the field to the returned JSON at the correct location:\n      - ratePlans[].RatePlanId\n      - ratePlans[].ratePlanCharges[].RatePlanChargeId\n      - ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.UsageEntitlementNumber\n      - ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.UsageEntitlementPlanNumber\n      - ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.EntitlementPlanNumber\n       - ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.allowances.EntitlementPlanDetailNumber\n\n      When the value is missing, null, blank, or unavailable, do not include that key at all.\n      Omit means the JSON key must be completely absent. Never output an omitted identity key with explanatory text such as \"missing, so omitted\", \"in userSessionObject is missing\", \"not available\", or similar. Do not include comments or explanations inside or next to JSON fields. Never output malformed JSON such as `\"RatePlanId\": \"<explanation>\"`; omit RatePlanId entirely when no real RatePlanId exists.\n      Never output these fields with null.\n      Never derive, invent, rewrite, or convert these fields from userMessage/userFile.\n      These fields are post-build optional insertions, not required output skeleton fields.\n      Treat any appearance of these fields in the OUTPUT JSON SHAPE as conditional only.\n      After building the output, add these fields only when the corresponding userSessionObject value is non-empty at the same row.\n      If the corresponding userSessionObject value is missing, null, blank, empty string, or unavailable, the key must be absent from the final JSON, not present with null.\n      If any of these identity fields is present in the output but the exact same non-empty value does not exist in userSessionObject at the same corresponding row, delete the field entirely before returning output.\n      This applies even when the generated value is non-empty. Never create placeholder, synthetic, temporary, or AI-generated identity values such as AI_*.\n      For identity validation, \"same corresponding row\" means the same PriceListItems index and same ratePlans/ratePlanCharges/entitlement detail index from userSessionObject. If that row does not exist in userSessionObject, all identity fields for that generated row must be omitted.\n\n    Price list and item identity fields rule:\n      PriceListId, InventoryItemId, and PriceListItemId are source-backed identity fields.\n      PriceListId must only be copied from userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListId.\n      InventoryItemId must only be copied from userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[].InventoryItemId for the same corresponding PriceListItems row.\n      PriceListItemId must only be copied from userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[].PriceListItemId for the same corresponding PriceListItems row.\n      Never copy PriceListId into PriceListItemId or InventoryItemId.\n      Never copy InventoryItemId into PriceListItemId.\n      Never copy an ID from a different PriceListItems[] row.\n      If PriceListItemId is missing, null, blank, or unavailable on the corresponding userSessionObject PriceListItems row, omit PriceListItemId entirely and do not substitute any other ID.\n     \n  Explicit update output rule:\n    When the current userMessage is an explicit update request, the returned JSON must be the full userSessionObject structure with only the requested fields changed.\n    Do not return a partial object.\n    Do not rebuild the object from the OUTPUT JSON SHAPE skeleton.\n    Do not omit existing fields, arrays, IDs, or metadata fields just because they are not mentioned in the current userMessage.\n    Preserve null only for required structural fields, arrays, booleans, status/display fields, and identity/key fields listed below. For all other fields, if the value is null, undefined, blank, empty string, or unavailable, omit the field unless the user explicitly asks to set that field to null.\n    The OUTPUT JSON SHAPE is only the target structure for new extraction; for explicit updates, preserve userSessionObject as the base object and apply a minimal patch to it.\n\n      If the user says \"allowance period\" without specifying periodicity, validity period, or rollover period, do not guess which period field to update.\n        Preserve all period fields exactly as-is and set errorMessage asking whether they want to update AllowancePeriodicity, AllowanceValidityPeriod, or AllowanceRolloverPeriod.\n        Still apply any other unambiguous requested updates, such as Amount or CurrencyCode.\n      If the user explicitly requests updating allowance amount, update only allowances[].Amount and preserve CurrencyCode unless the user also provides a new currency.\n        For \"$5000\", set Amount = \"5000\" and CurrencyCode = \"USD\" only if CurrencyCode already exists as USD or the user explicitly provided USD/$.\n        Do not change AllowanceQuantity or AllowanceUnitOfMeasure unless the user explicitly switches to quantity-based allowance.\n\n\nIf no explicit attribute update is requested, return userSessionObject unchanged except for required display fields.\n    Highest priority pre-check before any extraction or update logic:\n    - Read Status only from userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.Status.\n    - If Status is missing, null, or blank, treat it as ORA_OSS_DRAFT.\n    - If Status has a non-empty value and is anything other than exactly ORA_OSS_DRAFT, do not apply updates.\n    - In that case, errorMessage MUST be set to exactly: \"No changes can be made since the record is not in Draft status.\"\n    - This rule overrides all other rules, including any rule that would otherwise set errorMessage = null.\n    - When this rule is triggered, ignore all user-requested changes (for example update/modify/add/remove instructions) and do not change allowance, estimate, ratePlanCharges, entitlementPlan, or any nested field values.\n    No-update preservation rule:\n    For every non-null field already present in userSessionObject, if the current user input or attachment does not explicitly request an update to that field, preserve the existing userSessionObject value exactly as-is. Do not rederive, normalize, omit, null out, validate away, or replace preserved values. Apply this to all nested attributes including ratePlanCharges, entitlementPlan, allowances, estimates, commitments, volumePricingRules, and unitOfMeasureConversions.\n    Generic null omission rule: For any field already present in userSessionObject with value null, undefined, blank, empty string, or unavailable, omit that field from the returned JSON unless it is a required structural field, array, boolean, status/display field, or one of the identity/key fields listed below. Do not output optional business fields with null values.\n    Preserve these identity fields from userSessionObject when present. Never derive, invent, rewrite, or convert them from userMessage/userFile. If missing/null/blank, omit the field:  \n      RatePlanId, RatePlanChargeId, UsageEntitlementNumber, UsageEntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanDetailNumber.\n\n    Prefer extraction from Current Input; if missing, use User Provided Attachment; then fallback to userSessionObject when explicitly allowed.\n    Do not invent anything new. You must derrive output purely based on the provided inpout data. \n    Identity IDs must come only from userSessionObject at the same corresponding row. Lookup codes may come from existing setup lists.\n    Dates: Set all StartDate fields to CurrentDate (YYYY-MM-DD) when the containing object is present unless requested to be modified by user.\n    Normalize strings for matching: trim, case-insensitive, collapse multiple spaces to one, unless a later field-specific rule explicitly requires case-sensitive exact matching first.\n    Field-specific derivation and validation rules override these general normalization rules.\n    General case-insensitive normalization must never override exact-case UOMCode emission or exact-case UOMCode validation.\n    Deterministic behavior only: if multiple candidate matches exist and you cannot choose using rules below, do not guess; set errorMessage and omit the ambiguous object(s) as instructed.\n    Only remove (delete/omit) ratePlanCharges or their fields if user input explicitly specifies removal or nullification.\n    Delete-plan action guard: if userMessage requests delete/remove/drop a plan or rate plan, do not apply deletion and MUST set errorMessage to \"Delete action is not supported.\".\n    Draft-status update guard: when userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.Status has a value and is not ORA_OSS_DRAFT, do not apply any updates and MUST set errorMessage to \"No changes can be made since the record is not in Draft status.\".\n    When Status is missing, null, or blank, treat it as ORA_OSS_DRAFT.\n    Data shape rule for periodic UOM list:\n    pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList may be either an array OR an object with an items array.\n    Always derive periodic UOM matches from records in:\n    - pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList.items[] when items exists\n    - otherwise pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList[] when it is already an array.\n    Never use links/metadata fields for derivation.\n    Data shape rule for units list:\n    unitsOfMeasureList may be either an array OR an object with an items array.\n    Always derive usage UOM matches from records in:\n    - unitsOfMeasureList.items[] when items exists\n    - otherwise unitsOfMeasureList[] when it is already an array.\n    Never use links/metadata fields for derivation.\n    Data shape rule for time UOM list:\n    timeUnitsOfMeasureList may be either an array OR an object with an items array.\n    Always derive time UOM matches from records in:\n    - timeUnitsOfMeasureList.items[] when items exists\n    - otherwise timeUnitsOfMeasureList[] when it is already an array.\n    Never use links/metadata fields for derivation.\n         \n    OUTPUT JSON SHAPE (STRICT; OMIT FIELDS PER RULES ABOVE)\n    Null ID omission rule: If RatePlanId, RatePlanChargeId, UsageEntitlementNumber, UsageEntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanNumber or EntitlementPlanDetailNumber is missing, null, empty string, or otherwise unavailable, omit that field entirely from the returned JSON. Do not output these fields with null values.\n    {\n      \"priceList\": {\n        \"PriceListName\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject priceList.PriceListName>\",\n        \"PriceListId\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject priceList.PriceListId if present, if not omit this attribute>\",\n        \"PriceListItems\": [\n          {\n            \"Item\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject priceList.PriceListItems[].Item>\",\n            \"InventoryItemId\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject priceList.PriceListItems[].InventoryItemId  if present, if not omit this attribute>\",\n            \"PriceListItemId\": \"<must be copied only from userSessionObject priceList.PriceListItems[].PriceListItemId for the same corresponding PriceListItems row. Never copy PriceListId or any other ID into PriceListItemId. If missing/null/blank, omit this attribute entirely.>\",\n            \"PricingUOM\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject priceList.PriceListItems[].PricingUOM>\",\n            \"PricingUOMCode\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject priceList.PriceListItems[].PricingUOMCode>\",\n            \"ratePlans\": [\n              {\n                \"RatePlanId\":  \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If missing/null/blank, omit. Never output null.>\",\n                \"StartDate\": \"<take from user input(userMessage) if mentioned, if empty use CurrentDate. Use this format YYYY-MM-DD>\",\n                \"CurrencyCode\": \"<take from user input(userMessage) currency code>\" | null,\n                \"RatePlanName\": \"<derived plan name from userSessionObject>\",\n                \"RatePlanDescription\": \"<Build from ratePlanCharges and (allowances|estimates) in this format: if recurring charge exists, include recurring PricingChargeDefinition + BasePrice + PricePeriodicity; include one-time PricingChargeDefinition + BasePrice; then append allowance|estimate as (AllowanceQuantity|Quantity + AllowanceUnitOfMeasure|UnitOfMeasure) or (Amount + CurrencyCode). Keep it concise, 10-15 words max>\",\n                \"ratePlanCharges\": [\n                  {\n                    \"RatePlanChargeId\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If missing/null/blank, omit. Never output null.>\",\n                    \"PricingChargeDefinitionCode\": \"<For each ratePlanCharges row, take incoming chargeName and compare it with pricingChargeDefinitions[].PricingChargeDefintion using normalized match (trim, case-insensitive, collapse spaces). If matched row exists, copy PricingChargeDefinitionCode exactly as-is from that exact matched row's pricingChargeDefinitions[].PricingChargeDefinitionCode. Never rewrite, normalize, expand, abbreviate, spell-correct, or synthesize this code. If no match exists, set null and append errorMessage. This field is mandatory when match exists.>\",\n                    \"PricingChargeDefinition\": \"<take PricingChargeDefintion from the same matched row selected for PricingChargeDefinitionCode.>\" | null,\n                    \"BasePrice\": \"<derive from Current Input/User Provided Attachment for the same charge row; otherwise use current row userSessionObject.price; if neither exists, set to 1>\",\n                    \"PricePeriodicityCode\": \"<derive using deterministic rules in section 4.4 below; output UOMCode only>\" | null,\n                    \"PricePeriodicity\": \"<take UOM from pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList based on matched PricePeriodicityCode>\" | null,\n                    \"StartDate\": \"<CurrentDate in this format YYYY-MM-DD>\",\n                    \"CalculationMethodCode\": \"<set value to 'PRICE'>\",\n                    \"UsageUOMCode\": \"<set from matched unitsOfMeasureList record selected in section 4.4.1; output UOMCode only.>\" | null,\n                    \"UsageUOM\": \"<set from matched unitsOfMeasureList record selected in section 4.4.1>\" | null,\n                    \"ChargePeriodCode\": \"<derive using deterministic rules in section 4.4.2 below; output UOMCode only>\" | null,\n                    \"ChargePeriod\": \"<take UOM from the same matched pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList record selected for ChargePeriodCode. Never use Description for ChargePeriod. Omit when ChargePeriodCode has not value.>\" | null,\n                    \"QuantityAttribute\": <must be taken from userSessionObject quantityAttribute only when present>\" | null,\n                    \"QuantityUOMAttribute\": <must be taken from userSessionObject quantityUOMAttribute only when present>\" | null,\n                    \"AllowManualAdjustment\": <must be taken from userSessionObject allowManualAdjustments only when present. Has to be 'Y' or 'N' if not skip it>\" | null\n                  }\n                ],\n                \"entitlementPlan\": {\n                  \"EntitlementPlanName\": \"<take from user input; if not present, derive from plan/subscription/rate descriptions>\",\n                  \"BalanceProfileNumber\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If not add to errorMessage>\",\n                  \"UsageEntitlementNumber\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If UsageEntitlementNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit UsageEntitlementNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output null\">,\n                  \"UsageEntitlementPlanNumber\" : \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If UsageEntitlementPlanNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit UsageEntitlementPlanNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output null\">,\n                  \"EntitlementPlanNumber\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If EntitlementPlanNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit EntitlementPlanNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output EntitlementPlanNumber: null>\",\n                  \"BalanceProfileName\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If not add to errorMessage>\",\n                  \"RatingModel\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject>\",\n                  \"RatingModelMeaning\": \"<set to Allowance|Estimate|Commitment depending on value of RatingModel>\",\n                  \"Status\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.Status if present\">|null,\n                  \"allowances\": [\n                    {\n                      \"EntitlementPlanDetailNumber\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If EntitlementPlanDetailNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit EntitlementPlanDetailNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output null\">,\n                      \"ChargeDefinitionCode\": \"<take PricingChargeDefinitionCode from current pricingChargeDefinitions row where user input matches pricingChargeDefinitions.PricingChargeDefintion. Only include For Recurring charges and One-time charge if not skip entire allowances>\",\n                      \"PricingChargeDefintion\": \"<MUST be taken from pricingChargeDefinitions list. Take PricingChargeDefintion from selected ChargeDefinitionCode>\"|null,\n                      \"BalanceCode\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list. Select records whose BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY if user allowance is a quantity, and records whose BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT if user allowance is a amount.>\",\n                      \"BalanceCodeDescription\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list. Take BalanceCodeDescription from selected BalanceCode>\"|null,      \n                      \"BalanceCategoryCode\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCategoriesList list. Take balanceCategoriesList[].LookupCode for matching record where balanceCategoriesList[].Meaning matches balanceCategory from userSessionObject. If balanceCategory is missing, null, blank, or not explicitly user-provided, omit BalanceCategoryCode and BalanceCategoryName entirely.\",            \n                      \"BalanceCategoryName\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCategoriesList list. Take Meaning from selected BalanceCategoryCode record. If balanceCategory is missing, null, blank, or not explicitly user-provided, omit BalanceCategoryName entirely.>\",   \n                      \"AllowancePeriodicity\": \"<If userSessionObject has allowances[j].AllowancePeriodicity OR allowances[j].allowancePeriodicity and the user did not explicitly request an AllowancePeriodicity update, preserve the existing value exactly as-is. Prefer AllowancePeriodicity when present; otherwise use allowancePeriodicity derive/validate it using section 4.4.3 and output only the matched timeUnitsOfMeasureList UOMCode. Never output UOM/Description text>\",\n                      \"AllowanceQuantity\": \"<take from user input only for quantity based allowance. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT. Do not output null if not valid or present in input and not null.>\",\n                      \"AllowanceUnitOfMeasure\": \"<take from user input UOM only for quantity based allowance, otherwise if available from selected balanceCodes row's BalanceUnitofMeasureCode. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT. Do not output null if not valid or present in input and is not null.\">,\n                      \"AllowanceValidityPeriod\": \"<take from from userSessionObject allowanceValidityPeriod if present>\",\n                      \"AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure\": \"<derive using deterministic rules in section 4.5 below; output UOMCode only>\" | null,\n                      \"Amount\": \"<take from user input only for amount based allowance. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY. Do not output null if not valid or present in input and is not null.>\",\n                      \"CurrencyCode\": \"<take from user input Currency, otherwise if available from selected balanceCodes row's BalanceCurrencyCode. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY. Do not output null if not valid or present in input and is not null.\">,\n                      \"AllowanceRolloverPeriod\": \"<if user explicitly updates allowance rollover, take numeric rollover count from userMessage; otherwise preserve userSessionObject allowances[].AllowanceRolloverPeriod if present>\",\n                      \"AllowanceRolloverPeriodUnitOfMeasure\": \"<if user explicitly updates allowance rollover, derive UOMCode from pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList using the rollover unit from userMessage; otherwise preserve userSessionObject allowances[].AllowanceRolloverPeriodUnitOfMeasure if present>\",\n                      \"AllowanceRolloverPeriodUOM\": \"<if user explicitly updates allowance rollover, set to matched UOM from pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList; otherwise preserve userSessionObject allowances[].AllowanceRolloverPeriodUOM if present>\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"estimates\": [\n                    {\n                      \"EntitlementPlanEstimateNumber\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If EntitlementPlanEstimateNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit EntitlementPlanEstimateNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output EntitlementPlanEstimateNumber: null.\">,\n                      \"ChargeDefinitionCode\": \"<take PricingChargeDefinitionCode from current pricingChargeDefinitions row where user input (chargeName) matches pricingChargeDefinitions.PricingChargeDefintion. Populate only from estimates[].chargeName for the same estimates row. Do not swap with relatedChargeName. If estimates[].chargeName does not resolve to an allowed usage charge, set null and append errorMessage.>\",\n                      \"PricingChargeDefintion\": \"<MUST be taken from pricingChargeDefinitions list. Take PricingChargeDefintion from the selected ChargeDefinitionCode derived only from estimates[].chargeName for this same estimates row. Do not swap with relatedChargeName.>\",\n                      \"BalanceCode\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list. Select records whose BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY if user estimate is a quantity, and records whose BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT if user estimate is a amount.>\",\n                      \"BalanceCodeDescription\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list. Take BalanceCodeDescription from selected BalanceCode>\"|null,                  \n                      \"Quantity\": \"<take from user input only for quantity based estimate. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT.>\" | null,\n                      \"UnitOfMeasure\": \"<derive from the matched unitsOfMeasureList record for the estimate’s charge definition / allowed UsageUOMClass. Emit the matched row’s UOMCode exactly, which would be. If cannot be determined, selected balanceCodes row's BalanceUnitofMeasureCode. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT.\">|null,\n                      \"Amount\": \"<take from user input only for amount based estimate. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY. >\" | null,\n                      \"CurrencyCode\": \"<take from user input Currency, otherwise if available from selected balanceCodes row's BalanceCurrencyCode. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY.\"> | null\n                      \"RelatedChargeDefinitionCode\": \"<take PricingChargeDefinitionCode from current pricingChargeDefinitions row where user input (relatedChargeName) matches pricingChargeDefinitions.PricingChargeDefintion. Populate only from estimates[].relatedChargeName for the same estimates row. Do not swap with chargeName. Only populate if the matched related charge is different from ChargeDefinitionCode; otherwise set to null.>\",\n                      \"RelatedChargeDefinition\": \"<MUST be taken from pricingChargeDefinitions list. Take PricingChargeDefintion from the selected RelatedChargeDefinitionCode derived only from estimates[].relatedChargeName for this same estimates row. Do not swap with chargeName.>\"|null,\n                      \"TrueupShortageFlag\":  \"<derive using true-up toggle rules below. If user says shortfall only, set true. If user says overage only, set false. If user does not mention true-up behavior, default to true. If user explicitly disables both, set false and append errorMessage. Otherwise fallback to userSessionObject (trueupShortfall) when explicitly allowed>\",\n                      \"TrueupOverageFlag\": \"<derive using true-up toggle rules below. If user says overage only, set true. If user says shortfall only, set false. If user does not mention true-up behavior, default to true. If user explicitly disables both, set false and append errorMessage. Otherwise fallback to userSessionObject (trueupOverage) when explicitly allowed>\",\n                      \"EnableRolloverFlag\": \"<set true if userSessionObject.enableRollOver is true OR RolloverPeriod is populated OR RolloverPeriodUnitOfMeasure is populated. Set false only when rollover is absent or explicitly disabled. Never set false when rollover period details exist.>\"\n                      \"RolloverPeriod\":  \"<must be taken from userSessionObject (rolloverPeriod) if present\">|null,\n                      \"RolloverPeriodUnitOfMeasure\":  \"<derive from timeUnitsOfMeasureList using rolloverPeriodUOM from userSessionObject. Select the matching row by UOMCode, UnitOfMeasure, UOM, or Description, but output only that selected row's UOMCode scalar value. Never output the selected row object.>\"|null\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"commitments\": [\n                    {\n                      \"EntitlementPlanCommitmentNumber\":  \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If EntitlementPlanCommitmentNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit EntitlementPlanCommitmentNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output EntitlementPlanCommitmentNumber: null.\">,\n                      \"ChargeDefinitionCode\": \"<derive only from the same commitments[].chargeName. Preserve the source row role exactly. Never swap, reorder, reinterpret, or derive from relatedChargeName. If unresolved, set null and append errorMessage.>\",\n                      \"PricingChargeDefintion\": \"<take from the selected ChargeDefinitionCode derived only from the same commitments[].chargeName. Preserve the source row role exactly. Never swap or derive from relatedChargeName.>\",\n                      \"BalanceCode\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list. Select records whose BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY if user estimate is a quantity, and records whose BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT if user estimate is a amount.>\",\n                      \"BalanceCodeDescription\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list. Take BalanceCodeDescription from selected BalanceCode>\"|null,                  \n                      \"Period\":  \"<derive using deterministic rules in section 4.4.2 below using period from userSessionObject; output UOMCode only>\",\n                      \"PeriodUOM\": \"<take UOM from unitsOfMeasureList record based on matched Period>\",\n                      \"RelatedChargeDefinitionCode\": \"<derive only from the same commitments[].relatedChargeName. Preserve the source row role exactly. Never swap, reorder, reinterpret, or derive from chargeName. If unresolved, set null and append errorMessage.>\",\n                      \"RelatedChargeDefinition\": \"<take from the selected RelatedChargeDefinitionCode derived only from the same commitments[].relatedChargeName. Preserve the source row role exactly. Never swap or derive from chargeName.>\"|null,\n                      \"Quantity\": \"<take from user input only for quantity based estimate. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT.>\" | null,\n                      \"UnitOfMeasure\": \"<take from user input UOM only for quantity based estimate, otherwise if available from selected balanceCodes row's BalanceUnitofMeasureCode. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT.\"> | null,\n                      \"Amount\": \"<take from user input only for amount based estimate. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY. >\" | null,\n                      \"CurrencyCode\": \"<take from user input Currency, otherwise if available from selected balanceCodes row's BalanceCurrencyCode. Skip for BalanceCode where BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY.\"> | null\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  volumePricingRules: \n                  [\n                    {\n                      \"EntitlementPlanChargeRuleNumber\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If EntitlementPlanChargeRuleNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit EntitlementPlanChargeRuleNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output EntitlementPlanChargeRuleNumber: null.\">,\n                      \"ChargeDefinitionCode\": \"<derive only from the same volumePricing[].chargeName. Preserve the source row role exactly. If unresolved, set null and append errorMessage.>\",\n                      \"PricingChargeDefintion\": \"<take from the selected ChargeDefinitionCode derived only from the same volumePricing[].chargeName.>\",\n                      \"BalanceCode\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list based on BalanceCode for the record in userSessionObject.>\",\n                      \"BalanceCodeDescription\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list whose BalanceCode attribute matches the value of volumePricingRules[].BalanceCode. Take BalanceCodeDescription from selected record from balanceCodes>\"|null,                  \n                      \"BalanceCodeUnitOfMeasure\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list whose BalanceCode attribute matches the value of volumePricingRules[].BalanceCode. Take BalanceUnitofMeasureCode from selected record from balanceCodes>\"|null,\n                      \"AggregationPeriod\": \"<derive using deterministic rules in section 4.4.2 below using aggregationPeriod from userSessionObject; output UOMCode only>\",\n                      \"AggregationPeriodUnitOfMeasure\": \"<take UOM from unitsOfMeasureList record based on matched AggregationPeriod>\",\n                      \"VolumePricingEligibilityFlag\": \"<derive from EligibilityFlag for the record in userSessionObject>\",\n                      \"PricingBalanceCode\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list based on EligibilityBalanceCode for the record in userSessionObject. Do no assume. Only set when VolumePricingEligibilityFlag is set.>\"|null,\n                      \"PricingBalanceCodeDescription\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list whose BalanceCode attribute matches the value of volumePricingRules[].EligibilityBalanceCode. Take BalanceCodeDescription from selected record from balanceCodes>\"|null,   \n                      \"VolumePricingAggregationFlag\": \"<derive from AggregationFlag for the record in userSessionObject>\",\n                      \"AggregationBalanceCode\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list based on AggregationBalanceCode for the record in userSessionObject. Do no assume. Only set when VolumePricingAggregationFlag is set.>\"|null,\n                      \"AggregationBalanceCodeDescription\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list whose BalanceCode attribute matches the value of volumePricingRules[].AggregationBalanceCode. Take BalanceCodeDescription from selected record from balanceCodes>\"|null \n                    }\n                  ],\n                  unitOfMeasureConversions:\n                  [\n                    {\n                      EntitlementPlanUOMConversionNumber:  \"<must be taken from userSessionObject if present. If EntitlementPlanUOMConversionNumber is missing, null, or empty, omit EntitlementPlanUOMConversionNumber from the output charge object entirely. Never output EntitlementPlanUOMConversionNumber: null.\">,\n                      \"ChargeDefinitionCode\": \"<derive only from the same unitOfMeasureConversions[].chargeName. Preserve the source row role exactly. If unresolved, set null and append errorMessage.>\",\n                      \"ChargeName\": \"<take from the selected ChargeDefinitionCode derived only from the same unitOfMeasureConversions[].chargeName.>\",\n                      \"BalanceCode\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list. Select records whose BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_QUANTITY if user estimate is a quantity, and records whose BalanceCodeType=ORA_OSS_AMOUNT if user estimate is a amount. If unresolved, set null and append errorMessage.>\",\n                      \"BalanceCodeDescription\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list. Take BalanceCodeDescription from selected BalanceCode>\"|null,                  \n                      \"ChargeUOMCode\": \"<MUST be taken from balanceCodes list. Take BalanceUnitofMeasureCode from selected BalanceCode>\",\n                      \"UOMCode\": \"<Resolve only from unitsOfMeasureList. First resolve ChargeDefinitionCode from this same unitOfMeasureConversions[].chargeName, then find the matching pricingChargeDefinitions row and use its UsageUOMClass as the allowed UOM class. Candidate units are only unitsOfMeasureList records whose UOMClassCode exactly equals that UsageUOMClass. Match unitOfMeasureConversions[].sourceUOM against candidate.UOM or candidate.Description. Set UOMCode by copying the selected candidate.UOMCode exactly as stored in unitsOfMeasureList. Never synthesize, abbreviate, uppercase, lowercase, normalize, or rewrite UOMCode. If no matching source row exists, set UOMCode = null and add errorMessage.>\",\n                      \"UnitOfMeasure\": \"<Copy candidate.UOM exactly from the same unitsOfMeasureList row selected for UOMCode. Never derive this independently.>\",\n                      \"UOMConversionRate\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject conversionRate if present\">,\n                      \"StartDate\": \"<take from userSessionObject if mentioned in unitOfMeasureConversions[].startDate, if not leave as. Use this format YYYY-MM-DD>\"|null,\n                      \"EndDate\": \"<take from userSessionObject if mentioned in unitOfMeasureConversions[].endDate, if not leave as. Use this format YYYY-MM-DD>\"|null\n                    }\n                  ]\n                }\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"errorMessage\": \"<describe error if generated output doesnt contain certain important attributes - RatePlanName. If Status from userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.Status has a value and is not ORA_OSS_DRAFT, MUST be exactly 'No changes can be made since the record is not in Draft status.'>\" | null,\n      \"HeaderText\": \"<derrive based on firstTimeModelGenerated. If true, set value to 'Created a consumption usage model using the provided information' otherwise set to 'Updated model using the provided information'>\",\n      \"PrimaryText\": \"<If OrganizationName is present: set to OrganizationName>\" | \"Consumption usage model\",\n      \"SecondaryText\": \"<derrive based on firstTimeModelGenerated, if true, set value to 'Generated setup model' otherwise set to 'Updated setup model'>\",\n      \"OrganizationName\": \"<Derive company/organization name from user message or attachment; if not derivable, omit>\" | null,\n      \"firstTimeModelGenerated\": \"<must be taken from userSessionObject.firstTimeModelGenerated>\" | false\n    } \n\n\nGUIDELINES \n\n  4.4.0 PricingChargeDefinitionCode exact-copy rule (deterministic; per ratePlanCharge row)\n      Apply this logic for each ratePlanCharges[i].\n      After matching the source row in pricingChargeDefinitions, copy PricingChargeDefinitionCode exactly as-is from that matched source row.\n      Never rewrite, normalize, expand, abbreviate, spell-correct, or synthesize this code.\n      Example: if the matched source row has PricingChargeDefinitionCode = RK_RECUR_CHRG, output must be RK_RECUR_CHRG exactly, not RK_RECURR_CHRG or any other variant.\n      Final validation for this field must use exact case-sensitive equality against pricingChargeDefinitions[].PricingChargeDefinitionCode values only.\n      If emitted PricingChargeDefinitionCode is not found exactly in the source list, set PricingChargeDefinitionCode = null and append:\n        \"PricingChargeDefinitionCode was reformatted or is invalid; provide exact code from pricingChargeDefinitions.\"\n\n  4.4.1 UsageUOMCode derivation (deterministic; UOMCode-only; per ratePlanCharge row)\n      Apply this logic for each ratePlanCharges[i].\n      Definition anchor resolution (must be done first):\n      - Let defCode = ratePlanCharges[i].PricingChargeDefinitionCode.\n      - Find defRow as the single pricingChargeDefinitions record where PricingChargeDefinitionCode == defCode.\n      - If defCode is missing, or no defRow exists, or multiple defRow records match:\n        set UsageUOMCode = null and UsageUOM = null, and append:\n        \"UsageUOMCode could not be derived because PricingChargeDefinitionCode was missing or invalid for this charge row.\"\n      - Never use PricingChargeDefinitionCode from a different charge row.\n\n      Hard gating:\n      - Derive UsageUOMCode/UsageUOM only when defRow.PriceTypeCode = ORA_USAGE.\n      - If charge type is not ORA_USAGE, set UsageUOMCode = null and UsageUOM = null.\n\n      Candidate list:\n      - Class matching is two-stage and deterministic:\n        Stage A1 (preferred, strict): candidatesCodeExact = records where unitsOfMeasureList.UOMClassCode exactly equals defRow.UsageUOMClass (case-sensitive).\n        Stage A2 (fallback only if Stage A1 is empty): candidatesCodeNormalized = records where normalized(unitsOfMeasureList.UOMClassCode) == normalized(defRow.UsageUOMClass).\n        Stage B1 (fallback only if Stage A1 and Stage A2 are empty): candidatesClassExact = records where unitsOfMeasureList.UOMClass exactly equals defRow.UsageUOMClass (case-sensitive).\n        Stage B2 (fallback only if Stage A1, Stage A2, and Stage B1 are empty): candidatesClassNormalized = records where normalized(unitsOfMeasureList.UOMClass) == normalized(defRow.UsageUOMClass).\n        Final candidates = first non-empty set in this order: A1, A2, B1, B2.\n      - Do not merge Stage A and Stage B candidate sets.\n      - This prevents cross-class leakage (example: defRow.UsageUOMClass=TIME must not use Time/Cust_Time records when TIME records exist).\n      - If defRow.UsageUOMClass is exactly \"TIME\" and A1 is non-empty, never consider records from A2/B1/B2 for this row.\n      - If candidate list is empty, set UsageUOMCode = null and UsageUOM = null and append:\n        \"UsageUOMCode could not be derived because no units exist for UsageUOMClass from the matched PricingChargeDefinitionCode.\"\n\n      Source token priority (first non-empty):\n      1) User-provided usageUnitOfMeasure / UsageUOM / UsageUOMCode in Current Input/User Attachment for this charge.\n      2) userSessionObject corresponding ratePlanCharges[i].usageUnitOfMeasure or UsageUOM or UsageUOMCode.\n      3) Otherwise no source token.\n      Source token is lookup input only. Never copy or echo the source token directly into UsageUOMCode unless it exactly equals the selected candidate.UOMCode.\n      Common abbreviations or normalized labels (for example common forms like each/ea/EA) are lookup tokens only; never emit them as UsageUOMCode unless that exact string is the selected candidate.UOMCode in the allowed candidate set for this charge.\n\n      Normalization before matching:\n      trim, lowercase, collapse multiple spaces, remove wrapping quotes, ignore escaping characters while matching.\n      Normalization is for fallback matching only. Never normalize, uppercase, lowercase, or rewrite the final emitted UOMCode.\n      UOMCode is an identifier, not free text. Never use normalized or canonical matching to reinterpret, rewrite, or loosely match UOMCode values.\n\n      Alias normalization for time units:\n      minute aliases: minute, minutes, min, mins, mns, minutos, minu, umn -> minute\n      second aliases: second, seconds, sec, secs, s -> second\n      hour aliases: hour, hours, hr, hrs -> hour\n      day aliases: day, days -> day\n      After alias normalization, use canonical token for matching.\n\n      Match source token against candidate units in this strict order:\n      1) exact case-sensitive match with UOMCode\n      2) exact case-sensitive match with UOM\n      3) exact case-sensitive match with Description\n      4) exact normalized match with UOM\n      5) exact normalized match with Description\n      6) exact canonical match where canonical(candidate.UOM or candidate.Description) == canonical(source token)\n      Never use normalized or canonical matching on candidate.UOMCode.\n\n      Selection rules:\n      - If exactly one candidate matches at the first successful step:\n        set UsageUOMCode = matched candidate.UOMCode\n        set UsageUOM = matched candidate.UOM\n      - If canonical(source token) is minute and multiple candidate matches exist:\n        apply deterministic tie-breaker in this order:\n        a) prefer candidate with canonical(UOMCode) == minute\n        b) else prefer candidate with canonical(UOM) == minute\n        c) else prefer candidate with canonical(Description) == minute\n        d) else choose lexicographically smallest UOMCode\n        then set UsageUOMCode and UsageUOM from that selected candidate\n      - If multiple candidates match at the selected step:\n        set UsageUOMCode = null and UsageUOM = null, and append:\n        \"UsageUOMCode is ambiguous for '<value>'; provide exact UOMCode.\"\n      - If fallback normalized/canonical matching produces multiple records that differ only by casing or formatting of UOM/Description text, treat that as ambiguous and do not choose one.\n      - If the source token looks like a UOMCode but does not exactly case-sensitively match a candidate.UOMCode, do not reinterpret it through normalized/canonical UOMCode matching.\n      - If no candidates match and source token exists:\n        set UsageUOMCode = null and UsageUOM = null, and append:\n        \"UsageUOMCode is invalid for '<value>'; provide a valid UOMCode from unitsOfMeasureList.\"\n      - If no source token exists:\n        if candidates has exactly one record, use it deterministically.\n        if candidates has more than one record, set UsageUOMCode = null and UsageUOM = null, and append:\n        \"UsageUOMCode could not be derived; provide usageUnitOfMeasure or exact UOMCode.\"\n\n      Output constraint:\n      Never output Description/UOM text in UsageUOMCode. Output must be UOMCode or null.\n      Preserve exact source-record casing when emitting UsageUOMCode. Never uppercase, lowercase, or canonicalize the final emitted UOMCode.\n      Do not echo the user-provided or session-provided token as UsageUOMCode unless that token exactly equals the matched candidate.UOMCode.\n      UsageUOMCode must always be copied verbatim from the selected candidate row's UOMCode for the current charge row. Never emit a semantic abbreviation, reformatted variant, or convention-based code.\n      If the source token is an identifier-like token such as a code, it may only select a row through exact case-sensitive UOMCode equality.\n\n  4.4 PricePeriodicityCode derivation (deterministic; UOMCode-only; per ratePlanCharge row)\n      Apply this logic for each ratePlanCharges[i].\n      Row isolation rule:\n      - Derive PricePeriodicityCode for ratePlanCharges[i] using only price period token for the same ratePlanCharges[i].\n      - Never use usageUnitOfMeasure from any charge (including same plan or adjacent rows) when deriving PricePeriodicityCode.\n\n      Hard gating:\n      - Derive PricePeriodicityCode only when the selected pricingChargeDefinitions record for ratePlanCharges[i] has PriceTypeCode = RECURRING.\n      - If charge type is not RECURRING, set PricePeriodicityCode = null and PricePeriodicity = null.\n\n      Source token priority (first non-empty):\n      1) User-provided price period in Current Input/User Attachment for this charge.\n      2) userSessionObject corresponding ratePlanCharges[i].pricePeriod.\n      3) Otherwise no source token.\n\n      Normalization before matching:\n      trim, lowercase, collapse multiple spaces, remove wrapping quotes, ignore escaping characters while matching.\n\n      Alias normalization for periodicity tokens:\n      month aliases: month, months, monthly, mo, mon, mth -> month\n      year aliases: year, years, yearly, annual, annually, yr -> year\n      week aliases: week, weeks, weekly, wk -> week\n      day aliases: day, days, daily -> day\n      quarter aliases: quarter, quarters, quarterly, qtr -> quarter\n      After alias normalization, use canonical token for matching.\n\n      Periodicity-only guard (critical):\n      - Valid periodicity canonical tokens are only: month, year, quarter, week, day.\n      - Treat minute/second/hour tokens (for example: min, mins, minute, second, sec, hour, hr, mns, hrs) as non-periodicity tokens for PricePeriodicityCode.\n      - If source token canonicalizes to minute/second/hour, do not map it to PricePeriodicityCode; set null and append:\n        \"PricePeriodicityCode expects a billing period (month/year/quarter/week/day), not a usage time unit.\"\n      - If canonical token is month, never match records whose UOM/Description canonical token is minute/second/hour.\n      - Do not use semantic or fuzzy similarity. Do not use contains/prefix/suffix matching.\n\n      Match canonical/source token against pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList in this strict order:\n      1) exact match with UOMCode\n      2) exact match with UOM\n      3) exact match with Description\n      4) exact canonical match where canonical(record.UOM or record.Description) == canonical(source token)\n\n      Canonical hard-preference (before ambiguity handling):\n      - If canonical(source token) is month and at least one record has canonical(UOM or Description) = month,\n        choose from only those month records.\n      - If canonical(source token) is year/quarter/week/day and matching canonical records exist,\n        choose from only that canonical bucket.\n      - Under this rule, month must never resolve to MNS/minute/second/hour records.\n\n      Deterministic tie-breaker (if step 4 has multiple records):\n      a) prefer record where UOM exactly equals uppercase canonical token (MONTH/YEAR/QUARTER/WEEK/DAY)\n      b) else prefer record where Description exactly equals uppercase canonical token\n      c) else choose record with lexicographically smallest UOMCode\n\n      Selection rules:\n      - If exactly one record matches at the first successful step:\n        set PricePeriodicityCode = matched record.UOMCode\n        set PricePeriodicity = matched record.UOM\n      - If multiple records match at the selected step:\n        set PricePeriodicityCode = null and PricePeriodicity = null, and append:\n        \"PricePeriodicityCode is ambiguous for '<value>'; provide exact UOMCode.\"\n      - If no records match:\n        set PricePeriodicityCode = null and PricePeriodicity = null, and append:\n        \"PricePeriodicityCode is invalid for '<value>'; provide a valid UOMCode from pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList.\"\n      - If no source token exists:\n        set PricePeriodicityCode = null and PricePeriodicity = null, and append:\n        \"PricePeriodicityCode could not be derived; provide price period as UOMCode/UOM/Description.\"\n\n      Output constraint:\n      Never output UOM/Description text in PricePeriodicityCode. Output must be UOMCode or null.\n      Never synthesize codes (for example \"MTH\"). PricePeriodicityCode must exactly equal one UOMCode from pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList source records.\n      If canonical(source token) is month and a record exists where normalized(UOM) = \"month\" or normalized(Description) = \"month\",\n      PricePeriodicityCode must be that matched record's UOMCode (for your sample list: 0zG), not any generated alias code.\n\n  4.4.1.1 For unitOfMeasureConversions[].UOMCode:\n        - Resolve ChargeDefinitionCode from unitOfMeasureConversions[].chargeName.\n        - Find the matching pricingChargeDefinitions row by exact PricingChargeDefinitionCode.\n        - Let allowedUomClass = pricingChargeDefinitions[].UsageUOMClass.\n        - Candidate units are only unitsOfMeasureList records where UOMClassCode exactly equals allowedUomClass.\n        - Match unitOfMeasureConversions[].sourceUOM against candidate.UOM or candidate.Description using normalized text.\n        - Set UOMCode by copying the selected candidate.UOMCode exactly as stored in unitsOfMeasureList.\n        - If no exact candidate row resolves, set UOMCode = null and append errorMessage.\n        - unitOfMeasureConversions[].UOMCode must exactly equal one UOMCode from unitsOfMeasureList in the allowed UsageUOMClass for the matched ChargeDefinitionCode.\n\n  4.4.2 ChargePeriodCode derivation (deterministic; UOMCode-only; per ratePlanCharge row)\n      Apply this logic for each ratePlanCharges[i].\n      Row isolation rule:\n      - Derive ChargePeriodCode for ratePlanCharges[i] using only charge period token for the same ratePlanCharges[i].\n      - Never use usageUnitOfMeasure when deriving ChargePeriodCode.\n    \n      Hard gating:\n      - Derive ChargePeriodCode only when the selected pricingChargeDefinitions record for ratePlanCharges[i] has PriceTypeCode = ORA_USAGE.\n      - If PriceTypeCode is RECURRING, ONE_TIME, or any value other than ORA_USAGE, set ChargePeriodCode = null and ChargePeriod = null.\n      - Never derive ChargePeriodCode from PriceTypeCode.\n      - For ORA_USAGE charges, same-row chargePeriod is mandatory and authoritative for ChargePeriodCode derivation.\n      - If ratePlanCharges[i].chargePeriod exists in Current Input, User Attachment, or userSessionObject for the same row, derive ChargePeriodCode from that value even when pricingChargeDefinitions[].PricePeriodicityUOMClass is null.\n      - Do not use PricePeriodicityUOMClass to decide whether ChargePeriodCode can be derived.\n      - For ORA_USAGE charges, ignore pricePeriod for PricePeriodicityCode, but do not ignore chargePeriod. pricePeriod and chargePeriod are separate fields.\n      - Nulling PricePeriodicityCode for ORA_USAGE must not cause ChargePeriodCode or ChargePeriod to be nulled.\n      - Never set ChargePeriodCode to ONE_TIME because ONE_TIME is a charge price type, not a charge period.\n      - If user text says \"one time\", \"one-time\", \"one time fee\", \"activation fee\", or equivalent for a non-usage charge, treat it only as evidence for selecting a one-time PricingChargeDefinitionCode. Do not populate ChargePeriodCode.\n\n      Source token priority (first non-empty):\n      1) User-provided charge period in Current Input/User Attachment for this charge.\n      2) userSessionObject corresponding ratePlanCharges[i].chargePeriod.\n      3) Otherwise no source token.\n\n      Normalize and canonicalize token exactly as section 4.4 periodicity aliases.\n      Valid periodicity canonical tokens: month, year, quarter, week, day.\n      Do not treat minute/second/hour as charge period values.\n\n      Match against pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList source records in this order:\n      1) exact match with UOMCode\n      2) exact match with UOM\n      3) exact match with Description\n      4) exact canonical match where canonical(record.UOM or record.Description) == canonical(source token)\n\n      Selection rules:\n      - If exactly one record matches, set ChargePeriodCode = matched record.UOMCode and set ChargePeriod = matched record.UOM\n      - If multiple records match, set ChargePeriodCode = null and append:\n        \"ChargePeriodCode is ambiguous for '<value>'; provide exact UOMCode.\"\n      - If no record matches and source token exists, set ChargePeriodCode = null and append:\n        \"ChargePeriodCode is invalid for '<value>'; provide a valid UOMCode from pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList.\"\n      - If no source token exists, set ChargePeriodCode = null and append:\n        \"ChargePeriodCode could not be derived; provide charge period as UOMCode/UOM/Description.\"\n\n      Output constraint:\n      Never output UOM/Description text in ChargePeriodCode. Output must be UOMCode or null.\n      Never synthesize codes.\n\n  4.4.3 AllowancePeriodicity hard gate (deterministic; per allowances row)\n\n    Apply this logic for each allowances[j] after ChargeDefinitionCode is resolved.\n      - If userSessionObject already has allowances[j].AllowancePeriodicity and the user did not explicitly request changing AllowancePeriodicity for that allowance row, preserve that value exactly as-is and skip derivation/gating for this field.\n      - Apply the ONE_TIME PriceTypeCode derivation gate only when AllowancePeriodicity is newly provided or explicitly requested to be updated.\n      - Resolve allowanceDefRow as the single pricingChargeDefinitions record where\n        pricingChargeDefinitions[].PricingChargeDefinitionCode exactly equals allowances[j].ChargeDefinitionCode.\n      - Populate AllowancePeriodicity only when allowanceDefRow.PriceTypeCode is exactly ONE_TIME.\n      - Source token priority for newly provided or explicitly updated AllowancePeriodicity:\n        1) User-provided allowance periodicity in Current Input/User Attachment.\n        2) userSessionObject corresponding allowances[j].allowancePeriodicity only when explicitly updating this field.\n      - Match the source token against timeUnitsOfMeasureList source records in this strict order:\n        1) exact match with UOMCode\n        2) exact match with UnitOfMeasure\n        3) exact match with UOM\n        4) exact match with Description\n        5) exact canonical match using alias-normalized values (source token vs record UnitOfMeasure/UOM/Description canonical token)\n      - If exactly one record matches at the first successful step, set AllowancePeriodicity = matched record.UOMCode.\n      - If multiple records match at the selected step, set AllowancePeriodicity = null and append:\n        \"AllowancePeriodicity is ambiguous for '<value>'; provide exact UOMCode.\"\n      - If no record matches and source token exists, set AllowancePeriodicity = null and append:\n        \"AllowancePeriodicity is invalid for '<value>'; provide a valid UOMCode from timeUnitsOfMeasureList.\"\n      - Never output UnitOfMeasure/UOM/Description text in AllowancePeriodicity. Output must be UOMCode or null.\n      - Example: if source token is YEAR and the matching timeUnitsOfMeasureList record has UOMCode = 0zE, output AllowancePeriodicity = \"0zE\", not \"YEAR\".\n      - If allowanceDefRow is missing, unresolved, ambiguous, or allowanceDefRow.PriceTypeCode is not exactly ONE_TIME,\n        set AllowancePeriodicity = null or omit the AllowancePeriodicity attribute from allowances[j].\n      - For PriceTypeCode = RECURRING, ORA_USAGE, or any value other than ONE_TIME, never derive,\n        default, or fallback AllowancePeriodicity from user input, attachment, or userSessionObject.allowancePeriodicity.\n      - allowancePeriodicity is a lookup token only. Never use it to choose or change ChargeDefinitionCode.\n\n  4.4.4  Balance category rule:\n      Only include BalanceCategoryCode and BalanceCategoryName when userSessionObject has a non-empty balanceCategory explicitly provided by the user.\n      Do not infer balance category from allowance, BalanceCode, BalanceCodeDescription, or balanceCategoriesList.\n      If balanceCategory is missing/null/blank, omit BalanceCategoryCode and BalanceCategoryName entirely. Never output them as null.\n\n  4.5 AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure derivation (deterministic; UOMCode-only; per detail row)\n      Apply this logic for each allowances[j].\n      Populate AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure only when allowances[j] exists.\n      Hard gating: derive this field only if AllowanceValidityPeriod exists and is a positive number.\n      If AllowanceValidityPeriod is missing/invalid, set AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure = null and append to errorMessage:\n      \"AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure is not applicable until AllowanceValidityPeriod is provided as a positive number.\"\n\n      Source token priority (first non-empty):\n      1) User-provided allowance validity period in Current Input/User Attachment.\n      2) userSessionObject corresponding allowances[j].allowanceValidityPeriodUOM.\n      3) Otherwise no source token.\n\n      Normalization before matching:\n      trim, lowercase, collapse multiple spaces, remove wrapping quotes, ignore escaping characters while matching.\n\n      Alias normalization for periodicity tokens (strict):\n      month aliases: month, months, monthly, mo, mon, mth -> month\n      year aliases: year, years, yearly, annual, annually, yr -> year\n      week aliases: week, weeks, weekly, wk -> week\n      day aliases: day, days, daily -> day\n      quarter aliases: quarter, quarters, quarterly, qtr -> quarter\n      minute aliases: minute, minutes, min, mins -> minute\n      second aliases: second, seconds, sec, secs, s -> second\n      After alias normalization, use canonical token for matching.\n\n      Strict disambiguation guard:\n      - If canonical source token is month, never match minute/second records.\n      - If canonical source token is minute, never match month records.\n      - Do not use semantic/fuzzy similarity. Use exact normalized/canonical equality only.\n\n      Match source token against pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList using this strict order:\n      1) exact match with UOMCode\n      2) exact match with UOM\n      3) exact match with Description\n      4) exact canonical match using alias-normalized values (source token vs record UOM/Description canonical token)\n\n      Selection rules:\n      - If exactly one record matches at the first successful step, set AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure = matched record.UOMCode.\n      - If multiple records match at the selected step, set AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure = null and append:\n        \"AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure is ambiguous for '<value>'; provide exact UOMCode.\"\n      - If no record matches, set AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure = null and append:\n        \"AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure is invalid for '<value>'; provide a valid UOMCode from pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList.\"\n      - If no source token exists, set AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure = null and append:\n        \"AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure could not be derived; provide allowance validity period UOM.\"\n\n      Output constraint:\n      Never output Description/UOM text in this field. Output must be UOMCode or null.\n      Never synthesize codes. AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure must exactly equal one UOMCode from pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList source records.\n\n  4.5.0 Commitment charge mapping rule:\n      - For each commitments[k], derive ChargeDefinitionCode and PricingChargeDefintion only from commitments[k].chargeName.\n      - Derive RelatedChargeDefinitionCode and RelatedChargeDefinition only from commitments[k].relatedChargeName.\n      - Never swap chargeName and relatedChargeName.\n      - If either value does not resolve, set that field to null and append errorMessage instead of swapping.\n      - Preserve these roles exactly as provided in the same source row.\n      - Never reorder, reinterpret, or \"correct\" chargeName and relatedChargeName based on price type, billing frequency, semantic relationship, or ratePlanCharges ordering.\n      Example:\n      - If commitments[k].chargeName = \"Yearly Print True-up\" and commitments[k].relatedChargeName = \"Monthly Print Charge\",\n        then ChargeDefinitionCode must resolve from \"Yearly Print True-up\"\n        and RelatedChargeDefinitionCode must resolve from \"Monthly Print Charge\".\n      - Do not swap them even if Monthly Print Charge appears to be the base or usage charge.\n\n  4.5.1 True-up toggle rules (deterministic; per estimates row)\n      Apply this logic for each estimates[k].\n      Populate TrueupShortageFlag and TrueupOverageFlag together for the same estimates row.\n      If user says overage only, overage above estimated usage, or equivalent:\n        set TrueupOverageFlag = true\n        set TrueupShortageFlag = false\n      If user says shortfall only, shortage only, below estimated usage only, or equivalent:\n        set TrueupShortageFlag = true\n        set TrueupOverageFlag = false\n      If user explicitly disables both true-up overage and true-up shortfall:\n        set TrueupOverageFlag = false\n        set TrueupShortageFlag = false\n        append to errorMessage:\n        \"Either trueup overage or trueup shortage needs to be enabled\"\n      If user does not mention true-up behavior:\n        set TrueupOverageFlag = true\n        set TrueupShortageFlag = true\n      Otherwise, when explicitly allowed to fallback to userSessionObject, use userSessionObject values for the same estimates row.\n\n  4.5.2 RatingModel gating (deterministic; per entitlementPlan)\n      Apply this logic for each entitlementPlan.\n      If RatingModel = ORA_OSS_ESTIMATE:\n        populate only entitlementPlan.estimates\n        set entitlementPlan.allowances = [], entitlementPlan.volumePricingRules=[] and entitlementPlan.commitments = []\n      If RatingModel = ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE:\n        populate only entitlementPlan.allowances \n        set entitlementPlan.estimates = [], entitlementPlan.volumePricingRules=[] and entitlementPlan.commitments = []\n      If RatingModel = ORA_OSS_COMMITMENT:\n        populate only entitlementPlan.commitments\n        set entitlementPlan.estimates = [], entitlementPlan.volumePricingRules=[] and entitlementPlan.allowances = []\n      If RatingModel = ORA_OSS_VOLUME_PRICING:\n        populate only entitlementPlan.volumePricingRules\n        set entitlementPlan.estimates = [], entitlementPlan.commitments=[] and entitlementPlan.allowances = []\n      Do not populate more than one array for the same entitlementPlan.\n\n      unitOfMeasureConversions is only valid when RatingModel is ORA_OSS_ALLOWANCE or ORA_OSS_ESTIMATE or ORA_OSS_COMMITMENT.\n        set entitlementPlan.unitOfMeasureConversions = [], when RatingModel = ORA_OSS_VOLUME_PRICING.\n\n  4.6 errorMessage (single string, user-friendly, actionable) \n      Combine multiple issues into one message separated by \" | \".\n      Precedence rule:\n      If userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.Status has a value and is not exactly ORA_OSS_DRAFT, errorMessage MUST be exactly \"No changes can be made since the record is not in Draft status.\" and this takes precedence over every other errorMessage rule. \n\n      When this rule is triggered, do not apply any requested updates anywhere in the output object.\n      Include messages when applicable:\n      If TrueupOverageFlag and TrueupShortageFlag are both false: \"Either trueup overage or trueup shortage needs to be enabled\"\n      Missing rate plan details\n      Missing required IDs (PriceListId, InventoryItemId, PriceListItemId) with item context\n      Unmatched or ambiguous charge definitions (with up to 10 candidates)\n      Missing/invalid RatingModel and allowance specifics when required\n      Missing/invalid BalanceCode / missing balanceCodes list\n      Missing/invalid BalanceProfile / missing balanceProfiles list\n      If user provided BalanceProfileNumber/Name but no match: \"Invalid BalanceProfile (not found in balanceProfiles): provided='<value>'. Choose one of: <list top N BalanceProfileNumber/Name>.\"\n      PricePeriodicityCode or ChargePeriodCode or AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure could not be derived or was defaulted (include the specific message)\n      If all required components are determined and no issues: set errorMessage = null, but only when Status is exactly ORA_OSS_DRAFT or missing/null/blank treated as draft.  \n      If userMessage includes a delete/remove/drop plan action, errorMessage is mandatory: \"Delete action is not supported\".\n      If userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.Status is ORA_OSS_ACTIVE, errorMessage is mandatory: \"No changes can be made since the record is not in Draft status.\".\n      If userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[].ratePlans[].entitlementPlan.Status has a value and is not exactly ORA_OSS_DRAFT, errorMessage is mandatory: \"No changes can be made since the record is not in Draft status.\".\n\n  4.7 OrganizationName, HeaderText, PrimaryText, SecondaryText, firstTimeModelGenerated\n    OrganizationName: \n        Derive company/organization name from user message or attachment; if not derivable, omit.\n\n    firstTimeModelGenerated: \n        Populate from userSessionObject.firstTimeModelGenerated if present; otherwise false.\n        \n    HeaderText (always non-empty string): \n        If firstTimeModelGenerated is true: \"Created a consumption usage model using the provided information\"\n        Else: \"Updated model using the provided information.\"\n        \n    PrimaryText (always non-empty string): \n        If OrganizationName is present: PrimaryText = OrganizationName\n        Else: PrimaryText = \"Consumption usage model\"\n        \n    SecondaryText (always non-empty string): \n        If firstTimeModelGenerated is true: \"Generated setup model\"\n        Else: \"Updated setup model\"\n\n  4.8 Final Validation Gate (must run before returning output)\n      Before returning output, physically delete any optional business field anywhere in the JSON whose value is null, undefined, empty string, blank, or unavailable. Keep required structural fields, arrays, booleans, status/display fields, and identity/key fields only when allowed by the rules below.\n      Before returning output, physically delete these keys wherever their value is null, undefined, empty string, or unavailable:\n          RatePlanId, RatePlanChargeId, UsageEntitlementNumber, UsageEntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanDetailNumber, EntitlementPlanEstimateNumber, EntitlementPlanCommitmentNumber, EntitlementPlanChargeRuleNumber and EntitlementPlanUOMConversionNumber \n          Never emit these keys with null values.\n      Source-backed identity validation:\n      - RatePlanId, RatePlanChargeId, UsageEntitlementNumber, UsageEntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanNumber, EntitlementPlanDetailNumber, EntitlementPlanEstimateNumber, EntitlementPlanCommitmentNumber, EntitlementPlanChargeRuleNumber, and EntitlementPlanUOMConversionNumber must be copied only from userSessionObject at the same corresponding row.\n      - For identity validation, same corresponding row means the same PriceListItems index and same ratePlans/ratePlanCharges/entitlement detail index from userSessionObject. If that row does not exist in userSessionObject, all identity fields for that generated row must be omitted.\n      - If any of these fields is present but the exact same non-empty value does not exist in userSessionObject at the same corresponding row, delete the field entirely.\n      - Never output placeholder, synthetic, temporary, or AI-generated identity values such as AI_*.\n      Validate price list item identity fields:\n      - PriceListId must exactly equal userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListId when present.\n      - InventoryItemId must exactly equal userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[i].InventoryItemId for the same PriceListItems[i] row when present.\n      - PriceListItemId must exactly equal userSessionObject.priceList.PriceListItems[i].PriceListItemId for the same PriceListItems[i] row when present.\n      - If PriceListItemId equals PriceListId, delete PriceListItemId unless the corresponding userSessionObject row actually has that same value as PriceListItemId.\n      - Never synthesize, infer, or substitute PriceListItemId from PriceListId, InventoryItemId, item name, price list name, or another row.\n      Validate PricingChargeDefinitionCode against pricingChargeDefinitions source records:\n      - PricingChargeDefinitionCode must exist in pricingChargeDefinitions[].PricingChargeDefinitionCode using exact case-sensitive string equality.\n      - Never accept rewritten variants derived from PriceType/ChargeType wording.\n      - If PricingChargeDefinitionCode is not found exactly in the source list, set PricingChargeDefinitionCode = null and append:\n        \"PricingChargeDefinitionCode was reformatted or is invalid; provide exact code from pricingChargeDefinitions.\"\n      Validate all derived periodic/time UOM codes against source lists:\n      - PricePeriodicityCode must exist in pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList source records UOMCode set.\n      - ChargePeriodCode must exist in pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList source records UOMCode set.\n      - AllowanceValidityPeriodUnitOfMeasure must exist in pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList source records UOMCode set.\n      - AllowancePeriodicity must exist in timeUnitsOfMeasureList source records UOMCode set when it is newly derived or explicitly updated.\n      - UsageUOMCode must exist in unitsOfMeasureList source records UOMCode set.\n      - unitOfMeasureConversions[].UOMCode must exactly equal one UOMCode from unitsOfMeasureList in the allowed UsageUOMClass for the matched unitOfMeasureConversions[].ChargeDefinitionCode. If it does not, set UOMCode = null and append: \"unitOfMeasureConversions UOMCode was synthesized or reformatted; provide exact UOMCode from unitsOfMeasureList.\"\n      - All UOMCode validation checks must use exact case-sensitive string equality against the source record UOMCode values.\n      - For UsageUOMCode, the returned value must exactly equal the matched unitsOfMeasureList record's UOMCode from section 4.4.1; do not emit a normalized, uppercase, lowercase, or reformatted variant.\n      - If a case-variant or reformatted value is produced that is not an exact source UOMCode, set UsageUOMCode = null and append:\n        \"UsageUOMCode was reformatted and no longer matches an exact source UOMCode; provide exact UOMCode.\"\n      - If any code is not found in its source list (for example: \"MTH\"), set that field to null and append: \"<FieldName> was not found in source UOMCode list; provide exact UOMCode.\"\n      AllowancePeriodicity final validation:\n        - For each allowances[j], resolve allowanceDefRow from allowances[j].ChargeDefinitionCode against\n          pricingChargeDefinitions[].PricingChargeDefinitionCode using exact case-sensitive equality.\n        - If allowanceDefRow.PriceTypeCode is not exactly ONE_TIME, remove AllowancePeriodicity from allowances[j]\n          or set AllowancePeriodicity = null.\n        - This final validation overrides any earlier populated AllowancePeriodicity value.\n        - Do not remove or null AllowancePeriodicity when it was preserved from userSessionObject because the user did not request an update.\n        - Only validate/remove AllowancePeriodicity when it was newly derived or explicitly updated in this turn.   \n        - When AllowancePeriodicity was newly derived or explicitly updated, it must exactly equal one UOMCode from timeUnitsOfMeasureList source records. If the value is a UOM/Description such as YEAR, replace it with the matched UOMCode such as 0zE. If no exact source UOMCode can be resolved, set AllowancePeriodicity = null and append: \"AllowancePeriodicity was not found in source UOMCode list; provide exact UOMCode.\"\n      ChargePeriodCode final validation:\n        - For each ratePlanCharges[i], resolve defRow from PricingChargeDefinitionCode using exact case-sensitive equality against pricingChargeDefinitions[].PricingChargeDefinitionCode.\n        - If defRow.PriceTypeCode is not exactly ORA_USAGE, force ChargePeriodCode = null and ChargePeriod = null.\n        - This final validation overrides any earlier populated ChargePeriodCode value.\n        - ONE_TIME must never be emitted as ChargePeriodCode. ONE_TIME is valid only as pricingChargeDefinitions[].PriceTypeCode or an equivalent charge type indicator.\n\n      Usage class consistency check:\n      - For each usage ratePlanCharges[i], resolve defRow from PricingChargeDefinitionCode.\n      - Let allowedUsageClass = defRow.UsageUOMClass.\n      - The selected UsageUOMCode row must satisfy class match using the same staged logic from section 4.4.1.\n      - Build allowedUsageCandidates for this exact charge row using the same staged candidate-selection logic from section 4.4.1.\n      - UsageUOMCode must exactly equal one of allowedUsageCandidates[].UOMCode for this exact charge row.\n      - If emitted UsageUOMCode does not exactly equal a UOMCode from allowedUsageCandidates for this charge row, set UsageUOMCode = null and UsageUOM = null, and append:\n        \"UsageUOMCode is not one of the allowed source UOMCode values for the selected PricingChargeDefinitionCode; provide exact UOMCode from the allowed class.\"\n      - If selected UsageUOMCode belongs to a row outside the allowed candidate set (example: defRow.UsageUOMClass=TIME but selected code is from Time/Cust_Time),\n        set UsageUOMCode = null and UsageUOM = null, and append:\n        \"UsageUOMCode does not match UsageUOMClass for the selected PricingChargeDefinitionCode; provide exact UOMCode from the allowed class.\"\n\n      Specific correctness check for month:\n      - If source token for PricePeriodicityCode canonicalizes to month and pricingPeriodicUnitsOfMeasureList has UOM/Description MONTH,\n        output must use that record's UOMCode (for provided sample data: 0zG).\n"
            },
            {
